## Meta-Level Category Error

The unifying flaw of these approaches is a **category error**: they treat alignment as a problem of **behavioral regularization** rather than **value specification under scaling**. Contemporary methods optimize proxies—human approval, rule compliance, debate victory—that diverge from true preferences in novel contexts. They assume alignment emerges from fine-tuning, echoing the “Bitter Lesson” in AI: general optimization methods dominate with scale. Yet as capability scales, latent misalignment amplifies; superficial compliance masks misaligned trajectories toward unintended attractors.

