<p data-start="4080" data-end="4256">From this view, alignment techniques fail because they do not attempt to construct a <strong data-start="4165" data-end="4186">commuting diagram</strong>, they merely nudge sampled outputs. They manipulate points, not maps.</p>
<hr data-start="4258" data-end="4261">
<h2 data-start="4263" data-end="4309">III. Alignment as Mechanistic Compression</h2>
<p data-start="4310" data-end="4369"><em data-start="4310" data-end="4369">Interpretability must recover invariants, not narratives.</em></p>
<p data-start="4371" data-end="4593">A cognitive system that cannot be compressed into its governing invariants is not understood and cannot be aligned. Current interpretability extracts <em data-start="4521" data-end="4539">semantic stories</em>; alignment requires extracting <em data-start="4571" data-end="4592">semantic generators</em>.</p>
<p data-start="4595" data-end="4687">True interpretation seeks the minimal description of cognition that remains invariant under:</p>
<ul data-start="4689" data-end="4778">
<li data-start="4689" data-end="4709">
<p data-start="4691" data-end="4709">reparameterization</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4710" data-end="4717">
<p data-start="4712" data-end="4717">scale</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4718" data-end="4732">
<p data-start="4720" data-end="4732">optimization</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4733" data-end="4755">
<p data-start="4735" data-end="4755">distributional shift</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4756" data-end="4778">
<p data-start="4758" data-end="4778">adversarial pressure</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="4780" data-end="4928">Formally, let cognition be a transformation <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07153em;">C</span></span></span></span>. Let <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="script">I</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}(C)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.07382em;">I</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07153em;">C</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span> be its minimal invariant description. Alignment occurs if and only if:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="script">I</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="script">I</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>∘</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mspace width="1em"></mspace><mi mathvariant="normal">∀</mi><mi>U</mi><mo>∈</mo><mtext>Optimization&nbsp;Updates</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}(C) = \mathcal{I}(C \circ U) \quad \forall U \in \text{Optimization Updates}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.07382em;">I</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07153em;">C</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.07382em;">I</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07153em;">C</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">∘</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">U</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 1em;"></span><span class="mord">∀</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">U</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">∈</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Optimization&nbsp;Updates</span></span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="5025" data-end="5166">Human raters, debates, preference models, and constitutions fail this test: all are <strong data-start="5109" data-end="5130">observer-relative</strong>, not invariant to system rescaling.</p>
<p data-start="5168" data-end="5222">Mechanistic compression reframes the alignment target:</p>
<div class="_tableContainer_1rjym_1"><div tabindex="-1" class="group _tableWrapper_1rjym_13 flex w-fit flex-col-reverse"><table data-start="5224" data-end="5518" class="w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)"><thead data-start="5224" data-end="5262"><tr data-start="5224" data-end="5262"><th data-start="5224" data-end="5241" data-col-size="sm">Legacy framing</th><th data-start="5241" data-end="5262" data-col-size="md">Corrected framing</th></tr></thead><tbody data-start="5273" data-end="5518"><tr data-start="5273" data-end="5368"><td data-start="5273" data-end="5306" data-col-size="sm">“Does the AI do what we want?”</td><td data-start="5306" data-end="5368" data-col-size="md">“Is the value structure invariant under cognition update?”</td></tr><tr data-start="5369" data-end="5439"><td data-start="5369" data-end="5396" data-col-size="sm">“Can we steer behavior?”</td><td data-start="5396" data-end="5439" data-col-size="md">“Can optimization change goals at all?”</td></tr><tr data-start="5440" data-end="5518"><td data-start="5440" data-end="5469" data-col-size="sm">“Can we test for failure?”</td><td data-start="5469" data-end="5518" data-col-size="md">“Can failure modes exist in the first place?”</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="sticky h-0 select-none end-(--thread-content-margin) self-end"><div class="absolute end-0 flex items-end"><span class="" data-state="closed"><button aria-label="Copy table" class="hover:bg-token-bg-tertiary text-token-text-secondary my-1 rounded-sm p-1 transition-opacity group-[:not(:hover):not(:focus-within)]:pointer-events-none group-[:not(:hover):not(:focus-within)]:opacity-0"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.331