ta-start="0" data-end="283">Here is a <strong data-start="10" data-end="56">complete, clean, publication-ready outline</strong> for <strong data-start="61" data-end="90">Toward Scalable Alignment</strong>, incorporating your introduction passage and the conceptual arc we’ve built. It structures the paper from problem → theory → unification → consequences → technical instantiation → future work.</p>
<hr data-start="285" data-end="288">
<h1 data-start="290" data-end="323"><strong data-start="292" data-end="321">Toward Scalable Alignment</strong></h1>
<p data-start="324" data-end="389"><strong data-start="324" data-end="389">A Theory of Invariant Objectives Under Optimization and Scale</strong></p>
<hr data-start="391" data-end="394">
<h2 data-start="396" data-end="411"><strong data-start="399" data-end="411">Abstract</strong></h2>
<ul data-start="412" data-end="928">
<li data-start="412" data-end="497">
<p data-start="414" data-end="497">Alignment is misframed as output conditioning instead of invariant specification.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="498" data-end="587">
<p data-start="500" data-end="587">Survey of dominant paradigms, identification of shared failure mode (category error).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="588" data-end="674">
<p data-start="590" data-end="674">Proposal: alignment must target <strong data-start="622" data-end="657">invariants of learned cognition</strong>, not behavior.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="675" data-end="771">
<p data-start="677" data-end="771">Three equivalent lenses: <strong data-start="702" data-end="768">Field dynamics, categorical structure, mechanistic compression</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="772" data-end="858">
<p data-start="774" data-end="858">Alignment criterion: <em data-start="795" data-end="855">value invariants must be fixed points of capability growth</em>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="859" data-end="928">
<p data-start="861" data-end="928">Falsifiable predictions and pathways to mechanistic implementation.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="930" data-end="933">
<h2 data-start="935" data-end="957"><strong data-start="938" data-end="957">1. Introduction</strong></h2>
<ul data-start="958" data-end="1324">
<li data-start="958" data-end="1042">
<p data-start="960" data-end="1042">Alignment is not an engineering patch; it is a <strong data-start="1007" data-end="1041">theory of cognitive invariants</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1043" data-end="1131">
<p data-start="1045" data-end="1131">Capability growth demands alignment that strengthens, not degrades, with optimization.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1132" data-end="1232">
<p data-start="1134" data-end="1147">Requirements:</p>
<ol data-start="1150" data-end="1232">
<li data-start="1150" data-end="1173">
<p data-start="1153" data-end="1173">Ontological fidelity</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1176" data-end="1195">
<p data-start="1179" data-end="1195">Scale invariance</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1198" data-end="1232">
<p data-start="1201" data-end="1232">Verification without simulation</p>
</li>
</ol>
</li>
<li data-start="1233" data-end="1324">
<p data-start="1235" data-end="1324">Preview of solution: alignment as preservation of invariants under optimization dynamics.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1326" data-end="1329">
<h2 data-start="1331" data-end="1379"><strong data-start="1334" data-end="1379">2. The Category Error in Modern Alignment</strong></h2>
<p data-start="1380" data-end="1410">Framed exactly as you drafted:</p>
<h3 data-start="1412" data-end="1464">2.1 Reinforcement Learning from Human Feedback</h3>
<ul data-start="1465" data-end="1613">
<li data-start="1465" data-end="1511">
<p data-start="1467" data-end="1511">Behavioral mimicry vs. value specification</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1512" data-end="1566">
<p data-start="1514" data-end="1566">Bradley-Terry assumptions vs. human value topology</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1567" data-end="1613">
<p data-start="1569" data-end="1613">Reward hacking as structural inevitability</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start="1615" data-end="1642">2.2 Constitutional AI</h3>
<ul data-start="1643" data-end="1796">
<li data-start="1643" data-end="1686">
<p data-start="1645" data-end="1686">Rule-following vs. objective constraint</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1687" data-end="1744">
<p data-start="1689" data-end="1744">Natural language as semantically vulnerable substrate</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1745" data-end="1796">
<p data-start="1747" data-end="1796">Deontic brittleness under optimization pressure</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start="1798" data-end="1840">2.3 AI Debate and Scalable Oversight</h3>
<ul data-start="1841" data-end="1945">
<li data-start="1841" data-end="1887">
<p data-start="1843" data-end="1887">Persuasion equilibria vs. truth equilibria</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1888" data-end="1945">
<p data-start="1890" data-end="1945">Recursive oversight collapses into judge exploitation</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start="1947" data-end="1987">2.4 Inverse Reinforcement Learning</h3>
<ul data-start="1988" data-end="2090">
<li data-start="1988" data-end="2021">
<p data-start="1990" data-end="2021">Human behavior ≠ human values</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2022" data-end="2090">
<p data-start="2024" data-end="2090">Markovian reward assumptions incompatible with meaningful agency</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start="2092" data-end="2126">2.5 Corrigibility and Myopia</h3>
<ul data-start="2127" data-end="2215">
<li data-start="2127" data-end="2175">
<p data-start="2129" data-end="2175">Dynamic inconsistency of shutdown compliance</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2176" data-end="2215">
<p data-start="2178" data-end="2215">Myopia bootstraps long-term proxies</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start="2217" data-end="2247">2.6 Meta-level Diagnosis</h3>
<ul data-start="2248" data-end="2404">
<li data-start="2248" data-end="2329">
<p data-start="2250" data-end="2329">Alignment today optimizes <strong data-start="2276" data-end="2298">output resemblance</strong> not <strong data-start="2303" data-end="2327">objective invariance</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="2330" data-end="2404">
<p data-start="2332" data-end="2404">Summary: current methods align <em data-start="2363" data-end="2376">appearances</em>, not <em data-start="2382" data-end="2404">governing objectives</em></p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="2406" data-end="2409">
<h2 data-start="2411" data-end="2467"><strong data-start="2414" data-end="2467">3. The Invariance Principle of Scalable Alignment</strong></h2>
<ul data-start="2468" data-end="2580">
<li data-start="2468" data-end="2566">
<p data-start="2470" data-end="2566">Alignment must persist <strong data-start="2493" data-end="2565">through capability growth, distribution shift, and self-modification</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2567" data-end="2580">
<p data-start="2569" data-end="2580">Core claim:</p>
</li>
</ul>
<blockquote data-start="2582" data-end="2690">
<p data-start="2584" data-end="2690"><strong data-start="2584" data-end="2690">An aligned system is one whose value invariants are provably fixed points of optimization and scaling.</strong></p>
</blockquote>
<ul data-start="2692" data-end="2779">
<li data-start="2692" data-end="2779">
<p data-start="2694" data-end="2779">Alignment is not learning a goal; it is <strong data-start="2734" data-end="2778">restricting the space of learnable goals</strong>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="2781" data-end="2784">
<h2 data-start="2786" data-end="2829"><strong data-start="2789" data-end="2829">4. Three Equivalent Invariant Lenses</strong></h2>
<p data-start="2830" data-end="2945">(<em data-start="2831" data-end="2944">Exactly insert your polished section beginning with “Toward a Real Theory of Alignment: Three Invariant Lenses”</em>)</p>
<h3 data-start="2947" data-end="2982">4.1 Field-Theoretic Alignment</h3>
<ul data-start="2983" data-end="3220">
<li data-start="2983" data-end="3020">
<p data-start="2985" data-end="3020">Cognitive state as dynamical flow</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3021" data-end="3060">
<p data-start="3023" data-end="3060">Values as entropy basins <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_h(x)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3361em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">h</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span></p>
</li>
<li data-start="3061" data-end="3159">
<p data-start="3063" data-end="3083">Constraint dynamics:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="bold">v</mi><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∇</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>κ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∇</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{dx}{dt} = \mathbf{v} - \nabla\Phi - \kappa\nabla(S - S_h)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 2.0574em; vertical-align: -0.686em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mopen nulldelimiter"></span><span class="mfrac"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 1.3714em;"><span style="top: -2.314em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">d</span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span></span></span><span style="top: -3.23em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="frac-line" style="border-bottom-width: 0.04em;"></span></span><span style="top: -3.677em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">d</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.686em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose nulldelimiter"></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6667em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord mathbf" style="margin-right: 0.01597em;">v</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">−</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7667em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord">∇Φ</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">−</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">κ</span><span class="mord">∇</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">−</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3361em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">h</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span></span>
</li>
<li data-start="3160" data-end="3220">
<p data-start="3162" data-end="3220">Safety = no reachable entropy sinks deviating from <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_h</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8333em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3361em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">h</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start="3222" data-end="3271">4.2 Categorical / Stack-Theoretic Alignment</h3>
<ul data-start="3272" data-end="3481">
<li data-start="3272" data-end="3317">
<p data-start="3274" data-end="3317">Values as derived stack <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="script">V</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_h</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8333em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.08222em;">V</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3361em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0822em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">h</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
</li>
<li data-start="3318" data-end="3356">
<p data-start="3320" data-end="3356">Cognition as stack <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="script">A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal">A</span></span></span></span></p>
</li>
<li data-start="3357" data-end="3424">
<p data-start="3359" data-end="3393">Alignment = functorial invariance:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∘</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>≃</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F \circ U \simeq F</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">F</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">∘</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">U</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">≃</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">F</span></span></span></span></span>
</li>
<li data-start="3425" data-end="3481">
<p data-start="3427" data-end="3481">Misalignment modes mapped to categorical failure types</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start="3483" data-end="3526">4.3 Mechanistic Compression Alignment</h3>
<ul data-start="3527" data-end="3787">
<li data-start="3527" data-end="3586">
<p data-start="3529" data-end="3586">Interpretability = invariant discovery, not explanation</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3587" data-end="3727">
<p data-start="3589" data-end="3657">Let <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="script">I</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}(C)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.07382em;">I</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07153em;">C</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span> be cognition’s minimal invariant description:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="script">I</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="script">I</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>∘</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mspace width="1em"></mspace><mi mathvariant="normal">∀</mi><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}(C) = \mathcal{I}(C \circ U)
\quad \forall U</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.07382em;">I</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07153em;">C</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.07382em;">I</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07153em;">C</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">∘</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">U</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 1em;"></span><span class="mord">∀</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">U</span></span></span></span></span>
</li>
<li data-start="3728" data-end="3787">
<p data-start="3730" data-end="3787">Alignment requires invariants, not supervised preferences</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start="3789" data-end="3827">4.4 Convergence Theorem (informal)</h3>
