ect inclusion in the paper or LaTeX.</p>
<hr data-start="151" data-end="154">
<h1 data-start="156" data-end="211"><strong data-start="158" data-end="211">7A. Alignment as an Invariant Fixed-Point Theorem</strong></h1>
<p data-start="213" data-end="486">We now formalize alignment as a statement about <strong data-start="261" data-end="315">invariant preservation under optimization dynamics</strong>. This section provides the minimal theoretical skeleton: the dynamical system, the invariant, the obstruction modes, and the fixed-point condition guaranteeing alignment.</p>
<hr data-start="488" data-end="491">
<h2 data-start="493" data-end="549"><strong data-start="496" data-end="549">7A.1 Cognitive Optimization as a Dynamical System</strong></h2>
<p data-start="551" data-end="555">Let:</p>
<ul data-start="557" data-end="1228">
<li data-start="557" data-end="701">
<p data-start="559" data-end="701"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="script">X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.14643em;">X</span></span></span></span> be the internal state manifold of a cognitive system (parameters, activations, memories, latent goals, inference machinery).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="702" data-end="885">
<p data-start="704" data-end="885"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>:</mo><mi mathvariant="script">X</mi><mo>→</mo><mi mathvariant="script">X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_t : \mathcal{X} \to \mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8333em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">U</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2806em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.109em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">:</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.14643em;">X</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">→</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.14643em;">X</span></span></span></span> be the system’s <strong data-start="760" data-end="781">optimization flow</strong> at capability scale <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x