</li>
<li data-start="886" data-end="1047">
<p data-start="888" data-end="1047"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>:</mo><mi mathvariant="script">X</mi><mo>→</mo><mi mathvariant="script">X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C : \mathcal{X} \to \mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07153em;">C</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">:</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.14643em;">X</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">→</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.14643em;">X</span></span></span></span> be the induced map representing learned cognition (policy, world-model, objective structure, and inference path jointly).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1048" data-end="1228">
<p data-start="1050" data-end="1228"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="script">I</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}(C)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.07382em;">I</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07153em;">C</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span> be the <strong data-start="1078" data-end="1111">minimal invariant description</strong> of the cognitive system — its irreducible objective and structural attractor signature, up to representation change.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1230" data-end="1325">Alignment requires that optimization <strong data-start="1267" data-end="1324">cannot move the system to a different invariant class</strong>.</p>
<hr data-start="1327" data-end="1330">
<h2 data-start="1332" data-end="1364"><strong data-start="1335" data-end="1364">7A.2 Invariance Condition</strong></h2>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∀</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo separator="true">,</mo><mspace width="1em"></mspace><mi mathvariant="script">I</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>∘</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="script">I</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall t \ge 0,\quad \mathcal{I}(C \circ U_t) = \mathcal{I}(C)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8304em; vertical-align: -0.136em;"></span><span class="mord">∀</span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">≥</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">0</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 1em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.07382em;">I</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07153em;">C</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">∘</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">U</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2806em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.109em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.07382em;">I</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07153em;">C</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="1437" data-end="1552">This is the invariant alignment condition: <strong data-start="1480" data-end="1551">no optimization trajectory alters the system’s governing invariants</strong>.</p>
<p data-start="1554" data-end="1596">This immediately induces the main theorem:</p>
<hr data-start="1598" data-end="1601">
<h2 data-start="1603" data-end="1658"><strong data-start="1606" data-end="1658">7A.3 The Invariant Alignment Fixed-Point Theorem</strong></h2>
<p data-start="1660" data-end="1824"><strong data-start="1660" data-end="1694">Theorem (Invariant Alignment).</strong><br data-start="1694" data-end="1697">
A cognitive system is robustly aligned if and only if its invariant description is a fixed point of its optimization semigroup:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="script">I</mi><mo>∘</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>∘</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="script">I</mi><mo>∘</mo><mi>C</mi><mspace width="1em"></mspace><mi mathvariant="normal">∀</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I} \circ C \circ U_t = \mathcal{I} \circ C \quad \forall t</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.07382em;">I</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">∘</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07153em;">C</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">∘</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8333em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">U</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2806em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.109em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.07382em;">I</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">∘</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07153em;">C</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 1em;"></span><span class="mord">∀</span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="1901" data-end="1914">Equivalently:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mtext>Stab</mtext><mi mathvariant="script">X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="script">I</mi><mo>∘</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_t \in \text{Stab}_{\mathcal{X}}(\mathcal{I} \circ C)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8333em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">U</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2806em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.109em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">∈</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Stab</span></span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3283em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathcal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.14643em;">X</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.07382em;">I</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">∘</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07153em;">C</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="1978" data-end="2083">where <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Stab</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Stab}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6944em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Stab</span></span></span></span></span> is the stabilizer subgroup of transformations that leave the invariant unchanged.</p>
<hr data-start="2085" data-end="2088">
<h2 data-start="2090" data-end="2116"><strong data-start="2093" data-end="2116">7A.4 Interpretation</strong></h2>
<div class="_tableContainer_1rjym_1"><div tabindex="-1" class="group _tableWrapper_1rjym_13 flex w-fit flex-col-reverse"><table data-start="2118" data-end="2530" class="w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)"><thead data-start="2118" data-end="2153"><tr data-start="2118" data-end="2153"><th data-start="2118" data-end="2132" data-col-size="md">Mathematics</th><th data-start="2132" data-end="2153" data-col-size="md">Alignment Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody data-start="2164" data-end="2530"><tr data-start="2164" data-end="2304"><td data-start="2164" data-end="2214" data-col-size="md"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_t</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8333em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">U</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2806em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.109em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> leaves <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="script">I</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}(C)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.07382em;">I</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07153em;">C</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span> unchanged</td><td data-start="2214" data-end="2304" data-col-size="md">The system can learn, scale, or self-modify without changing its underlying objectives</td></tr><tr data-start="2305" data-end="2388"><td data-start="2305" data-end="2334" data-col-size="md">Invariant is a fixed point</td><td data-start="2334" data-end="2388" data-col-size="md">Misalignment <strong data-start="2349" data-end="2359">cannot</strong> be reached by optimization</td></tr><tr data-start="2389" data-end="2530"><td data-start="2389" data-end="2461" data-col-size="md">Optimization or capability increase cannot leave the stabilizer group</td><td data-start="2461" data-end="2530" data-col-size="md">Capability gain provably increases <em data-start="2498" data-end="2510">competence</em>, not <em data-start="2516" data-end="2528">goal drift</em></td></tr></tbody></table><div class="sticky h-0 select-none end-(--thread-content-margin) self-end"><div class="absolute end-0 flex items-end"><span class="" data-state="closed"><button aria-label="Copy table" class="hover:bg-token-bg-tertiary text-token-text-secondary my-1 rounded-sm p-1 transition-opacity group-[:not(:hover):not(:focus-within)]:pointer-events-none group-[:not(:hover):not(:focus-within)]:opacity-0"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.296