<hr data-start="4786" data-end="4789">
<h2 data-start="4791" data-end="4819"><strong data-start="4794" data-end="4819">7A.8 Core Corollaries</strong></h2>
<p data-start="4821" data-end="5085"><strong data-start="4821" data-end="4860">Corollary 1 (Reward Impossibility).</strong><br data-start="4860" data-end="4863">
No reward function <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(x)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.00773em;">R</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span> can guarantee alignment, because reward learning introduces gradient fields that alter invariants unless <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.00773em;">R</span></span></span></span> itself is invariant under all <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_t</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8333em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">U</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2806em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.109em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>, which is unachievable if <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.00773em;">R</span></span></span></span> is learnable.</p>
<p data-start="5087" data-end="5280"><strong data-start="5087" data-end="5136">Corollary 2 (Interpretability Insufficiency).</strong><br data-start="5136" data-end="5139">
Post-hoc interpretation does not preserve invariants; it is not in the stabilizer group of <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="script">I</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}(C)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.07382em;">I</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07153em;">C</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span> and cannot certify alignment.</p>
<p data-start="5282" data-end="5437"><strong data-start="5282" data-end="5321">Corollary 3 (Control vs Structure).</strong><br data-start="5321" data-end="5324">
Control of outputs does not imply control of invariants. Only structural invariants provide scale-safe alignment.</p>
<hr data-start="5439" data-end="5442">
<h2 data-start="5444" data-end="5463"><strong data-start="5447" data-end="5463">7A.9 Summary</strong></h2>
<div class="_tableContainer_1rjym_1"><div tabindex="-1" class="group _tableWrapper_1rjym_13 flex w-fit flex-col-reverse"><table data-start="5465" data-end="5894" class="w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)"><thead data-start="5465" data-end="5518"><tr data-start="5465" data-end="5518"><th data-start="5465" data-end="5501" data-col-size="md">Necessary Condition for Alignment</th><th data-start="5501" data-end="5518" data-col-size="md">What It Means</th></tr></thead><tbody data-start="5529" data-end="5894"><tr data-start="5529" data-end="5614"><td data-start="5529" data-end="5553" data-col-size="md">Invariants must exist</td><td data-start="5553" data-end="5614" data-col-size="md">System objective must have a compressed, irreducible core</td></tr><tr data-start="5615" data-end="5708"><td data-start="5615" data-end="5665" data-col-size="md">Invariants must be preserved under optimization</td><td data-start="5665" data-end="5708" data-col-size="md">Training cannot change or rotate values</td></tr><tr data-start="5709" data-end="5799"><td data-start="5709" data-end="5753" data-col-size="md">Misaligned invariants must be unreachable</td><td data-start="5753" data-end="5799" data-col-size="md">Misalignment is outside reachable topology</td></tr><tr data-start="5800" data-end="5894"><td data-start="5800" data-end="5843" data-col-size="md">Safety must be provable without sampling</td><td data-start="5843" data-end="5894" data-col-size="md">Guarantees come from structure, not observation</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="sticky h-0 select-none end-(--thread-content-margin) self-end"><div class="absolute end-0 flex items-end"><span class="" data-state="closed"><button aria-label="Copy table" class="hover:bg-token-bg-tertiary text-token-text-secondary my-1 rounded-sm p-1 transition-opacity group-[:not(:hover):not(:focus-within)]:pointer-events-none group-[:not(:hover):not(:focus-within)]:opacity-0"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="ht