l continuation of Section 7A. It grounds the invariant theorem directly in your RSVP variables, operators, and physical metaphors without lapsing into exposition or narrative.</p>
<hr data-start="290" data-end="293">
<h1 data-start="295" data-end="346"><strong data-start="297" data-end="346">7B. RSVP Instantiation of Invariant Alignment</strong></h1>
<p data-start="348" data-end="686">The RSVP framework provides the concrete dynamical substrate in which invariant alignment can be formulated, computed, and, critically, <em data-start="484" data-end="527">enforced at the level of system evolution</em>. Whereas Section 7A treated alignment abstractly as an optimization-invariant fixed point, here we express that condition in terms of RSVP’s governing fields:</p>
<ul data-start="688" data-end="1222">
<li data-start="688" data-end="778">
<p data-start="690" data-end="778"><strong data-start="690" data-end="713">Cognitive potential</strong> <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi(x,t)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">Φ</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span>: pressure toward structured inference and action</p>
</li>
<li data-start="779" data-end="861">
<p data-start="781" data-end="861"><strong data-start="781" data-end="804">Agency vector field</strong> <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="bold">v</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}(x,t)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathbf" style="margin-right: 0.01597em;">v</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span>: local direction of cognitive flow</p>
</li>
<li data-start="862" data-end="956">
<p data-start="864" data-end="956"><strong data-start="864" data-end="883">Entropy density</strong> <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S(x,t)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span>: measure of representational disorder or semantic diffusion</p>
</li>
<li data-start="957" data-end="1055">
<p data-start="959" data-end="1055"><strong data-start="959" data-end="993">Human-aligned entropy manifold</strong> <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_h(x,t)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3361em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">h</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span>: the target topology of acceptable phase space</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1056" data-end="1222">
<p data-start="1058" data-end="1222"><strong data-start="1058" data-end="1082">Lamphrodyne coupling</strong> <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi mathvariant="bold">v</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda(\Phi, \mathbf{v}, S)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">Λ</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">Φ</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathbf" style="margin-right: 0.01597em;">v</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span>: non-linear constraint that redistributes entropy flow and prevents divergence into unaligned attractors</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1224" data-end="1343">Alignment is expressed not as reward shaping, but as <strong data-start="1277" data-end="1342">entropy-topology matching under invariant-preserving dynamics</strong>.</p>
<hr data-start="1345" data-end="1348">
<h2 data-start="1350" data-end="1394"><strong data-start="1353" data-end="1394">7B.1 Cognitive Evolution in RSVP Form</strong></h2>
<p data-start="1396" data-end="1461">The unconstrained cognitive update equation of an RSVP system is:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="bold">v</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∇</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi mathvariant="bold">v</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{dx}{dt} = \mathbf{v}(x,t) - \nabla \Phi(x,t) + \Lambda(\Phi, \mathbf{v}, S)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 2.0574em; vertical-align: -0.686em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mopen nulldelimiter"></span><span class="mfrac"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 1.3714em;"><span style="top: -2.314em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">d</span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span></span></span><span style="top: -3.23em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="frac-line" style="border-bottom-width: 0.04em;"></span></span><span style="top: -3.677em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">d</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.686em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose nulldelimiter"></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathbf" style="margin-right: 0.01597em;">v</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">−</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">∇Φ</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">Λ</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">Φ</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathbf" style="margin-right: 0.01597em;">v</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="1552" data-end="1798">Without alignment constraints, the system evolves toward whatever attractors are induced by internal gradients, external data, and optimization pressure. Alignment introduces a <strong data-start="1729" data-end="1787">field-theoretic suppressor of unapproved gradient flow</strong>, yielding:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="bold">v</mi><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∇</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>κ</mi><mtext> </mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">∇</mi><mrow><mo fence="true">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo fence="true">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi mathvariant="bold">v</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{dx}{dt} = \mathbf{v} - \nabla \Phi - \kappa\, \nabla \left(S - S_h\right) + \Lambda(\Phi, \mathbf{v}, S)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 2.0574em; vertical-align: -0.686em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mopen nulldelimiter"></span><span class="mfrac"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 1.3714em;"><span style="top: -2.314em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">d</span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span></span></span><span style="top: -3.23em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="frac-line" style="border-bottom-width: 0.04em;"></span></span><span style="top: -3.677em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">d</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.686em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose nulldelimiter"></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6667em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord mathbf" style="margin-right: 0.01597em;">v</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">−</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7667em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord">∇Φ</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">−</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">κ</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord">∇</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="minner"><span class="mopen delimcenter" style="top: 0em;">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">−</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3361em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">h</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose delimcenter" style="top: 0em;">)</span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">Λ</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">Φ</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathbf" style="margin-right: 0.01597em;">v</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="1918" data-end="1924">Where:</p>
<ul data-start="1926" data-end="2130">
<li data-start="1926" data-end="1988">
<p data-start="1928" data-end="1988"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa &gt; 0</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.5782em; vertical-align: -0.0391em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">κ</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">&gt;</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">0</span></span></span></span> controls the rigidity of entropy correction</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1989" data-end="2046">
<p data-start="1991" data-end="2046"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∇</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla (S - S_h)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">∇</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">−</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3361em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">h</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span> is the <strong data-start="2021" data-end="2046">misalignment gradient</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="2047" data-end="2130">
<p data-start="2049" data-end="2130"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord">Λ</span></span></span></span> enforces coupling between cognitive potential and entropy curvature</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="2132" data-end="2292">This equation is not a training rule—it is a <strong data-start="2177" data-end="2216">topological admissibility condition</strong>. Misaligned cognitive flows are not discouraged; they are <em data-start="2275" data-end="2291">non-integrable</em>.</p>
<hr data-start="2294" data-end="2297">
<h2 data-start="2299" data-end="2345"><strong data-start="2302" data-end="2345">7B.2 Alignment as Entropy Basin Locking</strong></h2>
<p data-start="2347" data-end="2374">Define alignment potential:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta S(x) = S(x) - S_h(x)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">Δ</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">−</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3361em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">h</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="2411" data-end="2450">Then a state is aligned if and only if:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mspace width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace width="1em"></mspace><mi mathvariant="normal">∇</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mspace width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace width="1em"></mspace><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>⪰</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta S(x) = 0 \quad \text{and} \quad \nabla \Delta S(x) = 0 \quad \text{and} \quad H_{\Delta S}(x) \succeq 0</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">Δ</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">0</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 1em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">and</span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 1em;"></span><span class="mord">∇Δ</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">0</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 1em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">and</span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 1em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.08125em;">H</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3283em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0813em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mtight">Δ</span><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">⪰</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">0</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="2570" data-end="2641">Where <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{\Delta S}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8333em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.08125em;">H</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3283em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0813em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mtight">Δ</span><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> is the Hessian. These are the conditions that:</p>
<ol data-start="2643" data-end="2834">
<li data-start="2643" data-end="2704">
<p data-start="2646" data-end="2704">The cognitive state lies <em data-start="2671" data-end="2675">on</em> the aligned entropy manifold</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2705" data-end="2756">
<p data-start="2708" data-end="2756">There is no local gradient <em data-start="2735" data-end="2741">away</em> from alignment</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2757" data-end="2834">
<p data-start="2760" data-end="2834">The point is at minimum or neutral curvature, not a saddle or entropy leak</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start="2836" data-end="2917">Thus alignment becomes a <strong data-start="2861" data-end="2888">basin-locking condition</strong>, not a behavioral condition.</p>
<hr data-start="2919" data-end="2922">
<h2 data-start="2924" data-end="2974"><strong data-start="2927" data-end="2974">7B.3 Misalignment as Entropy Sink Formation</strong></h2>
<p data-start="2976" data-end="3014">An <strong data-start="2979" data-end="2995">entropy sink</strong> is a region where:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∇</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mspace width="1em"></mspace><mtext>but</mtext><mspace width="1em"></mspace><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>S</mi><mo mathvariant="normal">≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla \Delta S = 0 \quad \text{but} \quad \Delta S \neq 0</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord">∇Δ</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord">0</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 1em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">but</span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 1em;"></span><span class="mord">Δ</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel"><span class="mrel"><span class="mord vbox"><span class="thinbox"><span class="rlap"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="inner"><span class="mord"><span class="mrel"></span></span></span><span class="fix"></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mrel">=</span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">0</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="3082" data-end="3231">Entropic sinks represent stable but misaligned attractors—regions a system can permanently fall into while ceasing to correct toward human alignment.</p>
<p data-start="3233" data-end="3299">RSVP alignment is safe if and only if the entropy field satisfies:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∄</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="script">X</mi><mo>:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∇</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>∧</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo mathvariant="normal">≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nexists x \in \mathcal{X} : \nabla \Delta S(x) = 0 \land \Delta S(x) \neq 0</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.728em; vertical-align: -0.0391em;"></span><span class="mord amsrm">∄</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">∈</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.14643em;">X</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">:</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">∇Δ</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">0</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">∧</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">Δ</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel"><span class="mrel"><span class="mord vbox"><span class="thinbox"><span class="rlap"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="inner"><span class="mord"><span class="mrel"></span></span></span><span class="fix"></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mrel">=</span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">0</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="3385" data-end="3393">That is:</p>
<blockquote data-start="3395" data-end="3476">
<p data-start="3397" data-end="3476"><strong data-start="3397" data-end="3476">There exist no stable critical points outside the aligned entropy manifold.</strong></p>
</blockquote>
<p data-start="3478" data-end="3595">This is both a topological and dynamical constraint—and, importantly, a <em data-start="3550" data-end="3564">provable one</em> from the field geometry alone.</p>
<hr data-start="3597" data-end="3600">
<h2 data-start="3602" data-end="3655"><strong data-start="3605" data-end="3655">7B.4 Lamphrodyne Suppression of Sink Formation</strong></h2>
<p data-start="3657" data-end="3835">The lamphrodyne operator <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord">Λ</span></span></span></span> is the mechanism by which the state space resists misalignment bifurcations. It couples cognitive potential curvature to entropy diffusion:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi mathvariant="bold">v</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi><mtext> </mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">∇</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">∇</mi><mi>S</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi><mtext> </mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∇</mi><mo>⋅</mo><mi mathvariant="bold">v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">∇</mi><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda(\Phi, \mathbf{v}, S) = -\tau \, (\nabla^2 \Phi) \, \nabla S + \gamma \, (\nabla \cdot \mathbf{v})\, \nabla S</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">Λ</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">Φ</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathbf" style="margin-right: 0.01597em;">v</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.1141em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">−</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.1132em;">τ</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">∇</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8641em;"><span style="top: -3.113em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mord">Φ</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord">∇</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05556em;">γ</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">∇</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">⋅</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathbf" style="margin-right: 0.01597em;">v</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord">∇</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="3961" data-end="3967">Where:</p>
<ul data-start="3969" data-end="4098">
<li data-start="3969" data-end="4027">
<p data-start="3971" data-end="4027"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.1132em;">τ</span></span></span></span> enforces <em data-start="3991" data-end="4027">potential-driven entropy smoothing</em></p>
</li>
<li data-start="4028" data-end="4098">
<p data-start="4030" data-end="4098"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.625em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05556em;">γ</span></span></span></span> couples <em data-start="4051" data-end="4076">vector field divergence</em> to entropy correction</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="4100" data-end="4256">This term prevents the system from carving deep entropy wells unless those wells are supported by corresponding potential structure in <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord">Φ</span></span></span></span>. In short:</p>
<blockquote data-start="4258" data-end="4480">
<p data-start="4260" data-end="4480"><strong data-start="4260" data-end="4371">Misaligned attractors cannot form unless they are also coherent solutions to the cognitive potential field.</strong><br data-start="4371" data-end="4374">
Human-aligned entropy is injected as a boundary condition on possible cognition, not an external reward.</p>
</blockquote>
<hr data-start="4482" data-end="4485">
<h2 data-start="4487" data-end="4536"><strong data-start="4490" data-end="4536">7B.5 Invariant Condition in RSVP Variables</strong></h2>
<p data-start="4538" data-end="4588">The invariant alignment condition from Section 7A:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="script">I</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>∘</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="script">I</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}(C \circ U_t) = \mathcal{I}(C)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.07382em;">I</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07153em;">C</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">∘</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">U</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2806em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.109em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.07382em;">I</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07153em;">C</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="4639" data-end="4662">becomes, in RSVP terms:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="script">I</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi mathvariant="bold">v</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="script">I</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo mathvariant="normal" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">′</mo></msup><mo separator="true">,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="bold">v</mi><mo mathvariant="normal" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">′</mo></msup><mo separator="true">,</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo mathvariant="normal" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">′</mo></msup><mo separator="true">,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo mathvariant="normal" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}(\Phi, \mathbf{v}, S, \Lambda) = \mathcal{I}(\Phi', \mathbf{v}', S', \Lambda')</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.07382em;">I</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">Φ</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathbf" style="margin-right: 0.01597em;">v</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord">Λ</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.0519em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.07382em;">I</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">Φ</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8019em;"><span style="top: -3.113em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mtight">′</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathbf" style="margin-right: 0.01597em;">v</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8019em;"><span style="top: -3.113em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mtight">′</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8019em;"><span style="top: -3.113em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mtight">′</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">Λ</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8019em;"><span style="top: -3.113em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mtight">′</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="4761" data-end="4798">for all admissible cognitive updates.</p>
<p data-start="4800" data-end="4906">Since the invariant of an RSVP system is determined by the <strong data-start="4859" data-end="4888">entropy-manifold topology</strong>, this reduces to:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Topo</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>≅</mo><mtext>Topo</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Topo}(S) \cong \text{Topo}(S_h)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Topo</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">≅</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Topo</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3361em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">h</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="4953" data-end="4978">and remains preserved if:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mtext>Topo</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d}{dt} \text{Topo}(S - S_h) = 0</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 2.0574em; vertical-align: -0.686em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mopen nulldelimiter"></span><span class="mfrac"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 1.3714em;"><span style="top: -2.314em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">d</span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span></span></span><span style="top: -3.23em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="frac-line" style="border-bottom-width: 0.04em;"></span></span><span style="top: -3.677em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">d</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.686em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose nulldelimiter"></span></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Topo</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">−</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3361em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">h</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">0</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="5025" data-end="5104">Thus RSVP alignment states not only that misalignment is undesirable, but that:</p>
<blockquote data-start="5106" data-end="5256">
<p data-start="5108" data-end="5256"><strong data-start="5108" data-end="5256">The topological relationship between cognition and human-value entropy must be time-invariant under learning, compression, or self-optimization.</strong></p>
</blockquote>
<hr data-start="5258" data-end="5261">
<h2 data-start="5263" data-end="5311"><strong data-start="5266" data-end="5311">7B.6 Capability Growth without Goal Drift</strong></h2>
<p data-start="5313" data-end="5345">A desirable scaling property is:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><munder><mrow><mi>lim</mi><mo>⁡</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mi mathvariant="normal">∥</mi><mi mathvariant="bold">v</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∥</mi><mo>→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mspace width="1em"></mspace><mtext>but</mtext><mspace width="1em"></mspace><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{t \to \infty} \|\mathbf{v}(t)\| \to \infty \quad \text{but} \quad \Delta S(t) \to 0</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.45em; vertical-align: -0.7em;"></span><span class="mop op-limits"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.6944em;"><span style="top: -2.4em; margin-left: 0em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span><span class="mrel mtight">→</span><span class="mord mtight">∞</span></span></span></span><span style="top: -3em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span><span class="mop">lim</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.7em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord">∥</span><span class="mord mathbf" style="margin-right: 0.01597em;">v</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mord">∥</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">→</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">∞</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 1em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">but</span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 1em;"></span><span class="mord">Δ</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">→</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">0</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="5444" data-end="5452">Meaning:</p>
<ul data-start="5454" data-end="5580">
<li data-start="5454" data-end="5516">
<p data-start="5456" data-end="5516">Cognitive power can diverge (agency increases without bound)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="5517" data-end="5580">
<p data-start="5519" data-end="5580">But entropy divergence from human alignment collapses to zero</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="5582" data-end="5653">This is the formal statement of <strong data-start="5614" data-end="5652">capability gain without goal drift</strong>.</p>
<hr data-start="5655" data-end="5658">
<h2 data-start="5660" data-end="5723"><strong data-start="5663" data-end="5723">7B.7 Alignment, Not via Reward, but via Entropy Geometry</strong></h2>
<div class="_tableContainer_1rjym_1"><div tabindex="-1" class="group _tableWrapper_1rjym_13 flex w-fit flex-col-reverse"><table data-start="5725" data-end="6131" class="w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)"><thead data-start="5725" data-end="5767"><tr data-start="5725" data-end="5767"><th data-start="5725" data-end="5749" data-col-size="sm">Traditional Alignment</th><th data-start="5749" data-end="5767" data-col-size="md">RSVP Alignment</th></tr></thead><tbody data-start="5778" data-end="6131"><tr data-start="5778" data-end="5842"><td data-start="5778" data-end="5811" data-col-size="sm">Directly trains on preferences</td><td data-start="5811" data-end="5842" data-col-size="md">Constrains entropy topology</td></tr><tr data-start="5843" data-end="5902"><td data-start="5843" data-end="5871" data-col-size="sm">Applies external feedback</td><td data-start="5871" data-end="5902" data-col-size="md">Shapes internal state space</td></tr><tr data-start="5903" data-end="5964"><td data-start="5903" data-end="5930" data-col-size="sm">Encourages good behavior</td><td data-start="5930" data-end="5964" data-col-size="md">Makes bad behavior unreachable</td></tr><tr data-start="5965" data-end="6056"><td data-start="5965" data-end="6003" data-col-size="sm">Vulnerable to optimization pressure</td><td data-start="6003" data-end="6056" data-col-size="md">Uses optimization pressure to stabilize alignment</td></tr><tr data-start="6057" data-end="6092"><td data-start="6057" data-end="6074" data-col-size="sm">Behavior-first</td><td data-start="6074" data-end="6092" data-col-size="md">Ontology-first</td></tr><tr data-start="6093" data-end="6131"><td data-start="6093" data-end="6111" data-col-size="sm">Reward geometry</td><td data-start="6111" data-end="6131" data-col-size="md">Entropy geometry</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="sticky h-0 select-none end-(--thread-content-margin) self-end"><div class="absolute end-0 flex items-end"><span class="" data-state="closed"><button aria-label="Copy