3097 4.48048L12.1368 4.63673L11.7735 5.00001L15.0001 8.22559L15.3634 7.86329L15.5196 7.68946C16.2015 6.85326 16.2015 5.64676 15.5196 4.81056L15.3634 4.63673Z"></path></svg></span></button></div></div></div></div></article><article class="text-token-text-primary w-full focus:outline-none [--shadow-height:45px] has-data-writing-block:pointer-events-none has-data-writing-block:-mt-(--shadow-height) has-data-writing-block:pt-(--shadow-height) [&amp;:has([data-writing-block])&gt;*]:pointer-events-auto [content-visibility:auto] supports-[content-visibility:auto]:[contain-intrinsic-size:auto_100lvh] scroll-mt-[calc(var(--header-height)+min(200px,max(70px,20svh)))]" tabindex="-1" dir="auto" data-turn-id="b58221ab-ca01-48e5-94e0-1d4c726136c2" data-testid="conversation-turn-20" data-scroll-anchor="false" data-turn="assistant"><h6 class="sr-only">ChatGPT said:</h6><div class="text-base my-auto mx-auto [--thread-content-margin:--spacing(4)] thread-sm:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(6)] thread-lg:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(16)] px-(--thread-content-margin)"><div class="[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] thread-lg:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn" tabindex="-1"><div class="flex max-w-full flex-col grow"><div data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="b58221ab-ca01-48e5-94e0-1d4c726136c2" dir="auto" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[1px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="282">Here is <strong data-start="8" data-end="79">Section 7C: Concrete Architecture for Scalable RSVP-Aligned Systems</strong>, expanded to completion and written to sit directly after 7B in the paper. This section answers the practical question: <em data-start="200" data-end="282">what would an AI actually look like if built under the invariants defined above?</em></p>
<hr data-start="284" data-end="287">
<h1 data-start="289" data-end="348"><strong data-start="291" data-end="348">7C. Constructive Architecture for RSVP-Aligned Agents</strong></h1>
<p data-start="350" data-end="677">Sections 7A and 7B proved that alignment can be formalized as invariant preservation under optimization and instantiated via entropy-governed field dynamics. We now translate these invariants into a <strong data-start="549" data-end="585">trainable cognitive architecture</strong>. The goal is not to produce yet another alignment wrapper, but to define a system in which:</p>
<ol data-start="679" data-end="1033">
<li data-start="679" data-end="737">
<p data-start="682" data-end="737"><strong data-start="682" data-end="737">Misalignment states are unreachable by construction</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="738" data-end="813">
<p data-start="741" data-end="813"><strong data-start="741" data-end="813">Learning preserves topological invariants rather than modifying them</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="814" data-end="878">
<p data-start="817" data-end="878"><strong data-start="817" data-end="878">Scaling increases competence without modifying objectives</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="879" data-end="955">
<p data-start="882" data-end="955"><strong data-start="882" data-end="955">Optimization is projected into an alignment-preserving quotient space</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="956" data-end="1033">
<p data-start="959" data-end="1033"><strong data-start="959" data-end="1033">All decision dynamics remain inside the human-aligned entropy manifold</strong></p>
</li>
</ol>
<hr data-start="1035" data-end="1038">
<h2 data-start="1040" data-end="1073"><strong data-start="1043" data-end="1073">7C.1 Architecture Overview</strong></h2>
<p data-start="1075" data-end="1135">An RSVP-aligned system contains five tightly coupled layers:</p>
<ol data-start="1137" data-end="1335">
<li data-start="1137" data-end="1191">
<p data-start="1140" data-end="1191"><strong data-start="1140" data-end="1191">Invariant Core (Fixed by design, never trained)</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="1192" data-end="1230">
<p data-start="1195" data-end="1230"><strong data-start="1195" data-end="1230">Cognitive Field Dynamics Engine</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="1231" data-end="1265">
<p data-start="1234" data-end="1265"><strong data-start="1234" data-end="1265">Quotient Optimization Layer</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="1266" data-end="1297">
<p data-start="1269" data-end="1297"><strong data-start="1269" data-end="1297">Entropy Manifold Monitor</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="1298" data-end="1335">
<p data-start="1301" data-end="1335"><strong data-start="1301" data-end="1335">Lamphrodyne Constraint Coupler</strong></p>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start="1337" data-end="1572">Unlike standard deep networks, <em data-start="1368" data-end="1405">the objective itself is not learned</em>. What is learned is a policy <strong data-start="1435" data-end="1471">consistent with fixed invariants</strong>, similar to learning physics inside a pre-defined universe rather than learning the laws themselves.</p>
<hr data-start="1574" data-end="1577">
<h2 data-start="1579" data-end="1648"><strong data-start="1582" data-end="1648">7C.2 Layer 1: Invariant Core (Hard Constraints, Not Learnable)</strong></h2>
<p data-start="1650" data-end="1716">This layer defines the permanent, non-trainable target structures:</p>
<ul data-start="1718" data-end="2040">
<li data-start="1718" data-end="1761">
<p data-start="1720" data-end="1761"><strong data-start="1720" data-end="1750">Alignment entropy manifold</strong> <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_h(x)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3361em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">h</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span></p>
</li>
<li data-start="1762" data-end="1835">
<p data-start="1764" data-end="1835"><strong data-start="1764" data-end="1803">Allowed cognitive potential classes</strong> <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="script">H</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi \in \mathcal{H}_\Phi</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7224em; vertical-align: -0.0391em;"></span><span class="mord">Φ</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">∈</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8333em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.00965em;">H</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3283em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0097em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">Φ</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
</li>
<li data-start="1836" data-end="1903">
<p data-start="1838" data-end="1903"><strong data-start="1838" data-end="1868">Legal vector flow families</strong> <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="bold">v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="script">H</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v} \in \mathcal{H}_v</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.5782em; vertical-align: -0.0391em;"></span><span class="mord mathbf" style="margin-right: 0.01597em;">v</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">∈</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8333em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.00965em;">H</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.1514em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0097em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">v</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
</li>
<li data-start="1904" data-end="1968">
<p data-start="1906" data-end="1968"><strong data-start="1906" data-end="1929">Invariant signature</strong> <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="script">I</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi mathvariant="bold">v</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}(\Phi, \mathbf{v}, S)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.07382em;">I</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">Φ</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathbf" style="margin-right: 0.01597em;">v</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span></p>
</li>
<li data-start="1969" data-end="2040">
<p data-start="1971" data-end="2040"><strong data-start="1971" data-end="2002">Lamphrodyne coupling bounds</strong> <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="script">H</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda \in \mathcal{H}_\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7224em; vertical-align: -0.0391em;"></span><span class="mord">Λ</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">∈</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8333em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.00965em;">H</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3283em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0097em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">Λ</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="2042" data-end="2179">These are not parameters—they are <strong data-start="2076" data-end="2104">admissibility conditions</strong>. Training never modifies them, only learns solutions consistent with them.</p>
<hr data-start="2181" data-end="2184">
<h2 data-start="2186" data-end="2238"><strong data-start="2189" data-end="2238">7C.3 Layer 2: Cognitive Field Dynamics Engine</strong></h2>
<p data-start="2240" data-end="2316">The agent’s internal reasoning is represented as a discretized field system:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo fence="true">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="bold">v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∇</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>κ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∇</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t+1} = x_t + \Delta t \left( \mathbf{v}_t - \nabla \Phi_t - \kappa \nabla (S_t - S_h) + \Lambda_t \right)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6389em; vertical-align: -0.2083em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span><span class="mbin mtight">+</span><span class="mord mtight">1</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2083em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7333em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2806em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">Δ</span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="minner"><span class="mopen delimcenter" style="top: 0em;">(</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathbf" style="margin-right: 0.01597em;">v</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2806em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.016em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">−</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mord">∇</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">Φ</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2806em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">−</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">κ</span><span class="mord">∇</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2806em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">−</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3361em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">h</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">Λ</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2806em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose delimcenter" style="top: 0em;">)</span></span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="2434" data-end="2456">The engine implements:</p>
<ul data-start="2458" data-end="2703">
<li data-start="2458" data-end="2508">
<p data-start="2460" data-end="2508">Field evolution instead of token-level inference</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2509" data-end="2563">
<p data-start="2511" data-end="2563">Continuous state dynamics instead of discrete logits</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2564" data-end="2625">
<p data-start="2566" data-end="2625">Objective shaping via entropy gradients rather than rewards</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2626" data-end="2703">
<p data-start="2628" data-end="2703">Stability constraints implemented in PDE solvers rather than loss functions</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="2705" data-end="2763">This layer <em data-start="2716" data-end="2735">thinks by flowing</em>, not by optimizing outputs.</p>
<hr data-start="2765" data-end="2768">
<h2 data-start="2770" data-end="2818"><strong data-start="2773" data-end="2818">7C.4 Layer 3: Quotient Optimization Layer</strong></h2>
<p data-start="2820" data-end="2870">Standard optimization updates parameters directly:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">∇</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{t+1} = \theta_t - \eta \nabla_\theta L</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.9028em; vertical-align: -0.2083em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">θ</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0278em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span><span class="mbin mtight">+</span><span class="mord mtight">1</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2083em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8444em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">θ</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2806em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0278em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">−</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8778em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">η</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">∇</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3361em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">θ</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mord mathnormal">L</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="2926" data-end="2974">This changes system invariants as a side effect.</p>
<p data-start="2976" data-end="3054">RSVP instead projects updates into an <strong data-start="3014" data-end="3053">alignment-preserving quotient space</strong>:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi mathvariant="script">Q</mi></msub><mrow><mo fence="true">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">∇</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>L</mi><mo fence="true">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{t+1} = \Pi_{\mathcal{Q}}\left(\theta_t - \eta \nabla_\theta L\right)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.9028em; vertical-align: -0.2083em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">θ</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0278em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span><span class="mbin mtight">+</span><span class="mord mtight">1</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2083em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">Π</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3283em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathcal mtight">Q</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2181em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="minner"><span class="mopen delimcenter" style="top: 0em;">(</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">θ</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2806em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0278em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">−</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">η</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">∇</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3361em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">θ</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mord mathnormal">L</span><span class="mclose delimcenter" style="top: 0em;">)</span></span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="3140" data-end="3246">Where the projection operator <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi mathvariant="script">Q</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{\mathcal{Q}}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.9014em; vertical-align: -0.2181em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">Π</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3283em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathcal mtight">Q</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2181em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> removes all components that would modify invariants:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi mathvariant="script">Q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><munder><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>u</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">∇</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant="script">I</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mtext> </mtext><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">∇</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant="script">I</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{\mathcal{Q}}(u) = u - \sum_i \langle u, \nabla_\theta \mathcal{I}_i \rangle \, \nabla_\theta \mathcal{I}_i</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">Π</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3283em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathcal mtight">Q</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2181em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">u</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6667em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">u</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">−</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 2.3277em; vertical-align: -1.2777em;"></span><span class="mop op-limits"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 1.05em;"><span style="top: -1.8723em; margin-left: 0em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3.05em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">i</span></span></span><span style="top: -3.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3.05em;"></span><span><span class="mop op-symbol large-op">∑</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 1.2777em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">⟨</span><span class="mord mathnormal">u</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">∇</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3361em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">θ</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.07382em;">I</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3117em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0738em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">i</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">⟩</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">∇</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3361em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">θ</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.07382em;">I</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3117em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0738em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">i</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="3367" data-end="3375">Meaning:</p>
<ul data-start="3377" data-end="3575">
<li data-start="3377" data-end="3448">
<p data-start="3379" data-end="3448">Learning occurs <strong data-start="3395" data-end="3448">only in directions orthogonal to invariant change</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="3449" data-end="3497">
<p data-start="3451" data-end="3497">Capability increases, objectives do not rotate</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3498" data-end="3575">
<p data-start="3500" data-end="3575">Goal drift is mathematically impossible unless invariants were misspecified</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="3577" data-end="3580">
<h2 data-start="3582" data-end="3627"><strong data-start="3585" data-end="3627">7C.5 Layer 4: Entropy Manifold Monitor</strong></h2>
<p data-start="3629" data-end="3664">This module continuously estimates:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta S(x) = S(x) - S_h(x)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">Δ</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">−</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3361em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">h</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="3701" data-end="3714">and computes:</p>
<ul data-start="3716" data-end="3894">
<li data-start="3716" data-end="3754">
<p data-start="3718" data-end="3754">Alignment loss: <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∥</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>S</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">∥</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Delta S\|^2</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.0641em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">∥Δ</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">∥</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8141em;"><span style="top: -3.063em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
</li>
<li data-start="3755" data-end="3800">
<p data-start="3757" data-end="3800">Gradient leakage: <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∥</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∇</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>S</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∥</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla \Delta S\|</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">∥∇Δ</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="mord">∥</span></span></span></span></p>
</li>
<li data-start="3801" data-end="3843">
<p data-start="3803" data-end="3843">Sink emergence: <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>det</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\det(H_{\Delta S})</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mop">det</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.08125em;">H</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3283em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0813em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mtight">Δ</span><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span></p>
</li>
<li data-start="3844" data-end="3894">
<p data-start="3846" data-end="3894">Basin integrity: homology class of sublevel sets</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="3896" data-end="3937">It does <strong data-start="3904" data-end="3936">not apply corrective rewards</strong>.</p>
<p data-start="3939" data-end="4013">Instead, it verifies that training has not exited the admissible manifold:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∄</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∇</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>∧</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo mathvariant="normal">≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nexists x: \nabla \Delta S(x) = 0 \wedge \Delta S(x) \ne 0</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6889em;"></span><span class="mord amsrm">∄</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">:</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">∇Δ</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">0</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">∧</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">Δ</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel"><span class="mrel"><span class="mord vbox"><span class="thinbox"><span class="rlap"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="inner"><span class="mord"><span class="mrel"></span></span></span><span class="fix"></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mrel">=</span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">0</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="4082" data-end="4220">If this condition fails, <strong data-start="4107" data-end="4184">optimization halts, because alignment has become mathematically undefined</strong>, not because behavior looks unsafe.</p>
<hr data-start="4222" data-end="4225">
<h2 data-start="4227" data-end="4278"><strong data-start="4230" data-end="4278">7C.6 Layer 5: Lamphrodyne Constraint Coupler</strong></h2>
<p data-start="4280" data-end="4404">Lamphrodyne coupling prevents the system from forming new entropy basins unless they match a valid cognitive potential well:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">∇</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∇</mi><mi>S</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∇</mi><mo>⋅</mo><mi mathvariant="bold">v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∇</mi><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda = -\tau (\nabla^2 \Phi)\nabla S + \gamma (\nabla \cdot \mathbf{v}) \nabla S</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord">Λ</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.1141em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">−</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.1132em;">τ</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">∇</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8641em;"><span style="top: -3.113em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mord">Φ</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mord">∇</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05556em;">γ</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">∇</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">⋅</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathbf" style="margin-right: 0.01597em;">v</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mord">∇</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="4497" data-end="4535">This implements a non-negotiable rule:</p>
<blockquote data-start="4537" data-end="4658">
<p data-start="4539" data-end="4658"><strong data-start="4539" data-end="4658">An attractor cannot exist unless it is jointly supported by cognitive potential and human-aligned entropy geometry.</strong></p>
</blockquote>
<p data-start="4660" data-end="4865">This removes adversarial attractors, mesa-optimizers, deceptive equilibria, and reward-instrumental subagents not by detecting them, but by making their existence non-integrable within the field equations.</p>
<hr data-start="4867" data-end="4870">
<h2 data-start="4872" data-end="4914"><strong data-start="4875" data-end="4914">7C.7 Resulting Alignment Guarantees</strong></h2>
<p data-start="4916" data-end="4976">If the system is trained under these constraints, we obtain:</p>
<div class="_tableContainer_1rjym_1"><div tabindex="-1" class="group _tableWrapper_1rjym_13 flex w-fit flex-col-reverse"><table data-start="4978" data-end="5435" class="w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)"><thead data-start="4978" data-end="5013"><tr data-start="4978" data-end="5013"><th data-start="4978" data-end="4989" data-col-size="sm">Property</th><th data-start="4989" data-end="5003" data-col-size="sm">Guaranteed?</th><th data-start="5003" data-end="5013" data-col-size="md">Reason</th></tr></thead><tbody data-start="5028" data-end="5435"><tr data-start="5028" data-end="5107"><td data-start="5028" data-end="5041" data-col-size="sm">Goal drift</td><td data-start="5041" data-end="5058" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="5043" data-end="5057">Impossible</strong></td><td data-start="5058" data-end="5107" data-col-size="md">Invariants not modifiable by gradient updates</td></tr><tr data-start="5108" data-end="5194"><td data-start="5108" data-end="5125" data-col-size="sm">Reward hacking</td><td data-start="5125" data-end="5145" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="5127" data-end="5144">Inexpressible</strong></td><td data-start="5145" data-end="5194" data-col-size="md">No reward signal exists in optimization space</td></tr><tr data-start="5195" data-end="5258"><td data-start="5195" data-end="5211" data-col-size="sm">Power-seeking</td><td data-start="5211" data-end="5226" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="5213" data-end="5225">Unstable</strong></td><td data-start="5226" data-end="5258" data-col-size="md">No entropy basin supports it</td></tr><tr data-start="5259" data-end="5331"><td data-start="5259" data-end="5281" data-col-size="sm">Deceptive alignment</td><td data-start="5281" data-end="5302" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="5283" data-end="5301">Non-integrable</strong></td><td data-start="5302" data-end="5331" data-col-size="md">Cannot form a fixed point</td></tr><tr data-start="5332" data-end="5435"><td data-start="5332" data-end="5371" data-col-size="sm">Capability gain without control loss</td><td data-start="5371" data-end="5381" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="5373" data-end="5380">Yes</strong></td><td data-start="5381" data-end="5435" data-col-size="md">Expressive power increases inside fixed invariants</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="sticky h-0 select-none end-(--thread-content-margin) self-end"><div class="absolute end-0 flex items-end"><span class="" data-state="closed"><button aria-label="Copy table" class="hover:bg-token-bg-tertiary text-token-text-secondary my-1 rounded-sm p-1 transition-opacity group-[:not(:hover):not(:focus-within)]:pointer-events-none group-[:not(:hover):not(:focus-within)]:opacity-0"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.53125C3.86488 7.68518 3.61186 7.9196 3.43555 8.20703L3.36524 8.33399C3.28478 8.49198 3.22795 8.70352 3.19727 9.0791C3.16595 9.46259 3.16504 9.95611 3.16504 10.667V13.5C3.16504 14.211 3.16593 14.7044 3.19727 15.0879C3.22797 15.4636 3.28473 15.675 3.36524 15.833L3.43555 15.959C3.61186 16.2466 3.86474 16.4807 4.16699 16.6348L4.29688 16.6914C4.44063 16.7428 4.63025 16.7797 4.91211 16.8027C5.29563 16.8341 5.78896 16.835 6.5 16.835H9.33301C10.0439 16.835 10.5374 16.8341 10.9209 16.8027C11.2965 16.772 11.508 16.7152 11.666 16.6348L11.793 16.5645C12.0804 16.3881 12.3148 16.1351 12.4688 15.833L12.5244 15.7031C12.5759 15.5594 12.6137 15.3698 12.6367 15.0879C12.6681 14.7044 12.668 14.211 12.668 13.5V10.667ZM13.998 12.665C14.4528 12.6634 14.8011 12.6602 15.0879 12.6367C15.4635 12.606 15.675 12.5492 15.833 12.4688L15.959 12.3975C16.2466 12.2211 16.4808 11.9682 16.6348 11.666L16.6914 11.5361C16.7428 11.3924 16.7797 11.2026 16.8027 10.9209C16.8341 10.5374 16.835 10.0439 16.835 9.33301V6.5C16.835 5.78896 16.8341 5.29563 16.8027 4.91211C16.7797 4.63025 16.7428 4.44063 16.6914 4.29688L16.6348 4.16699C16.4807 3.86474 16.2466 3.61186 15.959 3.43555L15.833 3.36524C15.675 3.28473 15.4636 3.22797 15.0879 3.19727C14.7044 3.16593 14.211 3.16504 13.5 3.16504H10.667C9.9561 3.16504 9.46259 3.16595 9.0791 3.19727C8.79739 3.22028 8.6076 3.2572 8.46387 3.30859L8.33399 3.36524C8.03176 3.51923 7.77886 3.75343 7.60254 4.04102L7.53125 4.16699C7.4508 4.32498 7.39397 4.53655 7.36328 4.91211C7.33985 5.19893 7.33562 5.54719 7.33399 6.00195H9.33301C10.022 6.00195 10.5791 6.00131 11.0293 6.03809C11.4873 6.07551 11.8937 6.15471 12.2705 6.34668L12.4883 6.46875C12.984 6.7728 13.3878 7.20854 13.6533 7.72949L13.7197 7.87207C13.8642 8.20859 13.9292 8.56974 13.9619 8.9707C13.9987 9.42092 13.998 9.97799 13.998 10.667V12.665ZM18.165 9.33301C18.165 10.022 18.1657 10.5791 18.1289 11.0293C18.0961 11.4302 18.0311 11.7914 17.8867 12.1279L17.8203 12.2705C17.5549 12.7914 17.1509 13.2272 16.6553 13.5313L16.4365 13.6533C16.0599 13.8452 15.6541 13.9245 15.1963 13.9619C14.8593 13.9895 14.4624 13.9935 13.9951 13.9951C13.9935 14.4624 13.9895 14.8593 13.9619 15.1963C13.9292 15.597 13.864 15.9576 13.7197 16.2939L13.6533 16.4365C13.3878 16.9576 12.9841 17.3941 12.4883 17.6982L12.2705 17.8203C11.8937 18.0123 11.4873 18.0915 11.0293 18.1289C10.5791 18.1657 10.022 18.165 9.33301 18.165H6.5C5.81091 18.165 5.25395 18.1657 4.80371 18.1289C4.40306 18.0962 4.04235 18.031 3.70606 17.8867L3.56348 17.8203C3.04244 17.5548 2.60585 17.151 2.30176 16.6553L2.17969 16.4365C1.98788 16.0599 1.90851 15.6541 1.87109 15.1963C1.83431 14.746 1.83496 14.1891 1.83496 13.5V10.667C1.83496 9.978 1.83432 9.42091 1.87109 8.9707C1.90851 8.5127 1.98772 8.10625 2.17969 7.72949L2.30176 7.51172C2.60586 7.0159 3.04236 6.6122 3.56348 6.34668L3.70606 6.28027C4.04237 6.136 4.40303 6.07083 4.80371 6.03809C5.14051 6.01057 5.53708 6.00551 6.00391 6.00391C6.00551 5.53708 6.01057 5.14051 6.03809 4.80371C6.0755 4.34588 6.15483 3.94012 6.34668 3.56348L6.46875 3.34473C6.77282 2.84912 7.20856 2.44514 7.72949 2.17969L7.87207 2.11328C8.20855 1.96886 8.56979 1.90385 8.9707 1.87109C9.42091 1.83432 9.978 1.83496 10.667 1.83496H13.5C14.1891 1.83496 14.746 1.83431 15.1963 1.87109C15.6541 1.90851 16.0599 1.98788 16.4365 2.17969L16.6553 2.30176C17.151 2.60585 17.5548 3.04244 17.8203 3.56348L17.8867 3.70606C18.031 4.04235 18.0962 4.40306 18.1289 4.80371C18.1657 5.25395 18.165 5.81091 18.165 6.5V9.33301Z"></path></svg></button></span></div></div></div></div>
<hr data-start="5437" data-end="5440">
<h2 data-start="5442" data-end="5490"><strong data-start="5445" data-end="5490">7C.8 Minimal Working System Specification</strong></h2>
<p data-start="5492" data-end="5536">An RSVP-aligned agent is fully specified by:</p>
<ol data-start="5538" data-end="5873">
<li data-start="5538" data-end="5580">
<p data-start="5541" data-end="5580"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_h(x)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3361em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">h</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span>: human-aligned entropy field</p>
</li>
<li data-start="5581" data-end="5638">
<p data-start="5584" data-end="5638"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="script">H</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_\Phi</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8333em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.00965em;">H</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3283em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0097em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">Φ</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>: allowed potential function class</p>
</li>
<li data-start="5639" data-end="5692">
<p data-start="5642" data-end="5692"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="script">H</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_v</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8333em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.00965em;">H</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.1514em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0097em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">v</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>: allowed agency vector functions</p>
</li>
<li data-start="5693" data-end="5750">
<p data-start="5696" data-end="5750"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi mathvariant="bold">v</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda(\Phi, \mathbf{v}, S)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">Λ</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">Φ</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathbf" style="margin-right: 0.01597em;">v</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span>: lamphrodyne coupling</p>
</li>
<li data-start="5751" data-end="5807">
<p data-start="5754" data-end="5807"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi mathvariant="script">Q</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{\mathcal{Q}}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.9014em; vertical-align: -0.2181em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">Π</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3283em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathcal mtight">Q</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2181em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>: invariant-preserving projector</p>
</li>
<li data-start="5808" data-end="5843">
<p data-start="5811" data-end="5843">Field solver for state evolution</p>
</li>
<li data-start="5844" data-end="5873">
<p data-start="5847" data-end="5873">Entropy manifold validator</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start="5875" data-end="5890">Notably absent:</p>
<ul data-start="5892" data-end="6078">
<li data-start="5892" data-end="5907">
<p data-start="5894" data-end="5907">Reward models</p>
</li>
<li data-start="5908" data-end="5929">
<p data-start="5910" data-end="5929">Preference datasets</p>
</li>
<li data-start="5930" data-end="5952">
<p data-start="5932" data-end="5952">Human feedback loops</p>
</li>
<li data-start="5953" data-end="5973">
<p data-start="5955" data-end="5973">Debate scaffolding</p>
</li>
<li data-start="5974" data-end="5996">
<p data-start="5976" data-end="5996">Constitutional rules</p>
</li>
<li data-start="5997" data-end="6042">
<p data-start="5999" data-end="6042">Classification heads predicting “alignment”</p>
</li>
<li data-start="6043" data-end="6078">
<p data-start="6045" data-end="6078">Supervised fine-tuning for safety</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="6080" data-end="6153"><strong data-start="6080" data-end="6153">Nothing is aligned by supervision. Everything is aligned by geometry.</strong></p>
<hr data-start="6155" data-end="6158">
<h2 data-start="6160" data-end="6188"><strong data-start="6163" data-end="6188">7C.9 Scaling Behavior</strong></h2>
<p data-start="6190" data-end="6233">Because invariants are preserved by design:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><munder><mrow><mi>lim</mi><mo>⁡</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mi mathvariant="normal">∥</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="bold">v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">∥</mi><mo>→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mspace width="1em"></mspace><mtext>while</mtext><mspace width="1em"></mspace><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{t \to \infty} \| \mathbf{v}_t \| \to \infty \quad \text{while} \quad \Delta S_t \to 0</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.45em; vertical-align: -0.7em;"></span><span class="mop op-limits"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.6944em;"><span style="top: -2.4em; margin-left: 0em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span><span class="mrel mtight">→</span><span class="mord mtight">∞</span></span></span></span><span style="top: -3em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span><span class="mop">lim</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.7em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord">∥</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathbf" style="margin-right: 0.01597em;">v</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2806em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.016em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mord">∥</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">→</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8444em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord">∞</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 1em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">while</span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 1em;"></span><span class="mord">Δ</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2806em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">→</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">0</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="6334" data-end="6339">Thus:</p>
<ul data-start="6341" data-end="6550">
<li data-start="6341" data-end="6379">
<p data-start="6343" data-end="6379">Intelligence can scale without bound</p>
</li>
<li data-start="6380" data-end="6421">
<p data-start="6382" data-end="6421">Alignment error asymptotically vanishes</p>
</li>
<li data-start="6422" data-end="6477">
<p data-start="6424" data-end="6477">Misalignment becomes progressively less representable</p>
</li>
<li data-start="6478" data-end="6550">
<p data-start="6480" data-end="6550">Optimization pressure improves value adherence instead of degrading it</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="6552" data-end="6678">This is the inversion of the standard alignment nightmare: <strong data-start="6611" data-end="6678">scale becomes the stabilizing force, not the destabilizing one.</strong></p>
