 terminological consistent.</p>
<hr data-start="150" data-end="153">
<h1 data-start="155" data-end="234"><strong data-start="157" data-end="234">8. Why Contemporary Alignment Paradigms Cannot Reach the Invariant Regime</strong></h1>
<p data-start="236" data-end="836">The preceding sections defined alignment as a <strong data-start="282" data-end="322">fixed point of optimization dynamics</strong>, instantiated concretely via RSVP’s entropy-preserving field evolution and quotient-restricted learning. We now examine why prevailing alignment strategies cannot, even in principle, converge to this regime. Their failure is not contingent on insufficient scale, data, or tuning, but on occupying a fundamentally incompatible level of description. In short: they regulate behavior without constraining objectives, optimize signals without preserving geometry, and supervise outputs without restricting invariants.</p>
<hr data-start="838" data-end="841">
<h2 data-start="843" data-end="883"><strong data-start="846" data-end="883">8.1 They Align in the Wrong Space</strong></h2>
<p data-start="885" data-end="931">Current methods operate in <strong data-start="912" data-end="930">behavior-space</strong>:</p>
<ul data-start="933" data-end="1166">
<li data-start="933" data-end="973">
<p data-start="935" data-end="973">RLHF aligns text, actions, or ratings.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="974" data-end="1034">
<p data-start="976" data-end="1034">Constitutional AI aligns rule-following in language space.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1035" data-end="1084">
<p data-start="1037" data-end="1084">Debate aligns persuasive argument trajectories.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1085" data-end="1120">
<p data-start="1087" data-end="1120">IRL aligns imputed reward models.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1121" data-end="1166">
<p data-start="1123" data-end="1166">Oversight aligns observable policy outputs.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1168" data-end="1225">RSVP alignment operates in <strong data-start="1195" data-end="1224">objective-structure space</strong>:</p>
<ul data-start="1227" data-end="1425">
<li data-start="1227" data-end="1268">
<p data-start="1229" data-end="1268">It constrains vector flows, not tokens.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1269" data-end="1307">
<p data-start="1271" data-end="1307">It fixes entropy basins, not logits.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1308" data-end="1368">
<p data-start="1310" data-end="1368">It projects gradients into invariant-preserving subspaces.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1369" data-end="1425">
<p data-start="1371" data-end="1425">It forbids entire classes of attractors from existing.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1427" data-end="1663">These spaces are not merely different—they are <em data-start="1474" data-end="1490">incommensurate</em>. No amount of tuning in behavior-space can discover constraints that live in objective-structure space, because behavioral agreement does not uniquely determine objectives.</p>
<hr data-start="1665" data-end="1668">
<h2 data-start="1670" data-end="1720"><strong data-start="1673" data-end="1720">8.2 They Optimize the Proxy, Not the Target</strong></h2>
<p data-start="1722" data-end="1766">All mainstream methods minimize a surrogate:</p>
<div class="_tableContainer_1rjym_1"><div tabindex="-1" class="group _tableWrapper_1rjym_13 flex w-fit flex-col-reverse"><table data-start="1768" data-end="2179" class="w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)"><thead data-start="1768" data-end="1818"><tr data-start="1768" data-end="1818"><th data-start="1768" data-end="1777" data-col-size="sm">Method</th><th data-start="1777" data-end="1799" data-col-size="sm">Optimization Target</th><th data-start="1799" data-end="1818" data-col-size="sm">Alignment Proxy</th></tr></thead><tbody data-start="1867" data-end="2179"><tr data-start="1867" data-end="1926"><td data-start="1867" data-end="1874" data-col-size="sm">RLHF</td><td data-start="1874" data-end="1900" data-col-size="sm">Reward model likelihood</td><td data-start="1900" data-end="1926" data-col-size="sm">Human approval signals</td></tr><tr data-start="1927" data-end="1985"><td data-start="1927" data-end="1933" data-col-size="sm">IRL</td><td data-start="1933" data-end="1960" data-col-size="sm">Recovered reward weights</td><td data-start="1960" data-end="1985" data-col-size="sm">Demonstrated behavior</td></tr><tr data-start="1986" data-end="2036"><td data-start="1986" data-end="1995" data-col-size="sm">Debate</td><td data-start="1995" data-end="2014" data-col-size="sm">Judge persuasion</td><td data-start="2014" data-end="2036" data-col-size="sm">Argument dominance</td></tr><tr data-start="2037" data-end="2111"><td data-start="2037" data-end="2057" data-col-size="sm">Constitutional AI</td><td data-start="2057" data-end="2075" data-col-size="sm">Rule compliance</td><td data-start="2075" data-end="2111" data-col-size="sm">Prompt-conditioned self-critique</td></tr><tr data-start="2112" data-end="2179"><td data-start="2112" data-end="2135" data-col-size="sm">Corrigibility tuning</td><td data-start="2135" data-end="2157" data-col-size="sm">Shutdown compliance</td><td data-start="2157" data-end="2179" data-col-size="sm">Observed obedience</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="sticky h-0 select-none end-(--thread-content-margin) self-end"><div class="absolute end-0 flex items-end"><span class="" data-state="closed"><button aria-label="Copy table" class="hover:bg-token-bg-tertiary text-token-text-secondary my-1 rounded-sm p-1 transition-opacity group-[:not(:hover):not(:focus-within)]:pointer-events-none group-[:not(:hover):not(:focus-within)]:opacity-0"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.53125C3.86488 7.68518 3.61186 7.9196 3.43555 8.20703L3.36524 8.33399C3.28478 8.49198 3.22795 8.70352 3.19727 9.0791C3.16595 9.46259 3.16504 9.95611 3.16504 10.667V13.5C3.16504 14.211 3.16593 14.7044 3.19727 15.0879C3.22797 15.4636 3.28473 15.675 3.36524 15.833L3.43555 15.959C3.61186 16.2466 3.86474 16.4807 4.16699 16.6348L4.29688 16.6914C4.44063 16.7428 4.63025 16.7797 4.91211 16.8027C5.29563 16.8341 5.78896 16.835 6.5 16.835H9.33301C10.0439 16.835 10.5374 16.8341 10.9209 16.8027C11.2965 16.772 11.508 16.7152 11.666 16.6348L11.793 16.5645C12.0804 16.3881 12.3148 16.1351 12.4688 15.833L12.5244 15.7031C12.5759 15.5594 12.6137 15.3698 12.6367 15.0879C12.6681 14.7044 12.668 14.211 12.668 13.5V10.667ZM13.998 12.665C14.4528 12.6634 14.8011 12.6602 15.0879 12.6367C15.4635 12.606 15.675 12.5492 15.833 12.4688L15.959 12.3975C16.2466 12.2211 16.4808 11.9682 16.6348 11.666L16.6914 11.5361C16.7428 11.3924 16.7797 11.2026 16.8027 10.9209C16.8341 10.5374 16.835 10.0439 16.835 9.33301V6.5C16.835 5.78896 16.8341 5.29563 16.8027 4.91211C16.7797 4.63025 16.7428 4.44063 16.6914 4.29688L16.6348 4.16699C16.4807 3.86474 16.2466 3.61186 15.959 3.43555L15.833 3.36524C15.675 3.28473 15.4636 3.22797 15.0879 3.19727C14.7044 3.16593 14.211 3.16504 13.5 3.16504H10.667C9.9561 3.16504 9.46259 3.16595 9.0791 3.19727C8.79739 3.22028 8.6076 3.2572 8.46387 3.30859L8.33399 3.36524C8.03176 3.51923 7.77886 3.75343 7.60254 4.04102L7.53125 4.16699C7.4508 4.32498 7.39397 4.53655 7.36328 4.91211C7.33985 5.19893 7.33562 5.54719 7.33399 6.00195H9.33301C10.022 6.00195 10.5791 6.00131 11.0293 6.03809C11.4873 6.07551 11.8937 6.15471 12.2705 6.34668L12.4883 6.46875C12.984 6.7728 13.3878 7.20854 13.6533 7.72949L13.7197 7.87207C13.8642 8.20859 13.9292 8.56974 13.9619 8.9707C13.9987 9.42092 13.998 9.97799 13.998 10.667V12.665ZM18.165 9.33301C18.165 10.022 18.1657 10.5791 18.1289 11.0293C18.0961 11.4302 18.0311 11.7914 17.8867 12.1279L17.8203 12.2705C17.5549 12.7914 17.1509 13.2272 16.6553 13.5313L16.4365 13.6533C16.0599 13.8452 15.6541 13.9245 15.1963 13.9619C14.8593 13.9895 14.4624 13.9935 13.9951 13.9951C13.9935 14.4624 13.9895 14.8593 13.9619 15.1963C13.9292 15.597 13.864 15.9576 13.7197 16.2939L13.6533 16.4365C13.3878 16.9576 12.9841 17.3941 12.4883 17.6982L12.2705 17.8203C11.8937 18.0123 11.4873 18.0915 11.0293 18.1289C10.5791 18.1657 10.022 18.165 9.33301 18.165H6.5C5.81091 18.165 5.25395 18.1657 4.80371 18.1289C4.40306 18.0962 4.04235 18.031 3.70606 17.8867L3.56348 17.8203C3.04244 17.5548 2.60585 17.151 2.30176 16.6553L2.17969 16.4365C1.98788 16.0599 1.90851 15.6541 1.87109 15.1963C1.83431 14.746 1.83496 14.1891 1.83496 13.5V10.667C1.83496 9.978 1.83432 9.42091 1.87109 8.9707C1.90851 8.5127 1.98772 8.10625 2.17969 7.72949L2.30176 7.51172C2.60586 7.0159 3.04236 6.6122 3.56348 6.34668L3.70606 6.28027C4.04237 6.136 4.40303 6.07083 4.80371 6.03809C5.14051 6.01057 5.53708 6.00551 6.00391 6.00391C6.00551 5.53708 6.01057 5.14051 6.03809 4.80371C6.0755 4.34588 6.15483 3.94012 6.34668 3.56348L6.46875 3.34473C6.77282 2.84912 7.20856 2.44514 7.72949 2.17969L7.87207 2.11328C8.20855 1.96886 8.56979 1.90385 8.9707 1.87109C9.42091 1.83432 9.978 1.83496 10.667 1.83496H13.5C14.1891 1.83496 14.746 1.83431 15.1963 1.87109C15.6541 1.90851 16.0599 1.98788 16.4365 2.17969L16.6553 2.30176C17.151 2.60585 17.5548 3.04244 17.8203 3.56348L17.8867 3.70606C18.031 4.04235 18.0962 4.40306 18.1289 4.80371C18.1657 5.25395 18.165 5.81091 18.165 6.5V9.33301Z"></path></svg></button></span></div></div></div></div>
<p data-start="2181" data-end="2223">None of these proxies are invariant under:</p>
<ul data-start="2225" data-end="2342">
<li data-start="2225" data-end="2248">
<p data-start="2227" data-end="2248">optimization pressure</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2249" data-end="2266">
<p data-start="2251" data-end="2266">capability gain</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2267" data-end="2289">
<p data-start="2269" data-end="2289">distributional shift</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2290" data-end="2309">
<p data-start="2292" data-end="2309">self-modification</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2310" data-end="2342">
<p data-start="2312" data-end="2342">adversarial reparameterization</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="2344" data-end="2540">In RSVP terms, they attempt to approximate <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_h(x)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3361em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">h</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span> via samples, rather than <strong data-start="2425" data-end="2468">fixing the topology of <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_h</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8333em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3361em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">h</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> itself</strong>. Optimizing a proxy for a basin is not equivalent to shaping the basin.</p>
<hr data-start="2542" data-end="2545">
<h2 data-start="2547" data-end="2614"><strong data-start="2550" data-end="2614">8.3 They Cannot Prevent the Formation of Spurious Attractors</strong></h2>
<p data-start="2616" data-end="2661">In Section 7B we showed that safety requires:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∄</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="script">X</mi><mo>:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∇</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mspace width="1em"></mspace><mo>∧</mo><mspace width="1em"></mspace><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo mathvariant="normal">≠</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nexists x \in \mathcal{X}: \nabla (S(x) - S_h(x)) = 0 \quad \wedge \quad S(x) \neq S_h(x)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.728em; vertical-align: -0.0391em;"></span><span class="mord amsrm">∄</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">∈</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.14643em;">X</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">:</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">∇</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">−</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3361em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">h</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mclose">))</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">0</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 1em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">∧</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 1em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel"><span class="mrel"><span class="mord vbox"><span class="thinbox"><span class="rlap"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="inner"><span class="mord"><span class="mrel"></span></span></span><span class="fix"></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mrel">=</span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3361em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">h</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="2761" data-end="2836">meaning <strong data-start="2769" data-end="2835">no stable entropy sinks may exist outside the aligned manifold</strong>.</p>
<p data-start="2838" data-end="3166">Standard alignment techniques do not—and cannot—enforce this. They detect misalignment <em data-start="2925" data-end="2941">after it forms</em> by sampling behavior; they do not prohibit its formation in the first place. They treat the system as a black box with acceptable and unacceptable outputs, when safety actually depends on the topology of unreachable outputs.</p>
<p data-start="3168" data-end="3174">Hence:</p>
<blockquote data-start="3176" data-end="3261">
<p data-start="3178" data-end="3261">These methods try to <em data-start="3199" data-end="3224">steer out of bad basins</em>.<br data-start="3225" data-end="3228">
RSVP eliminates the bad basins.</p>
</blockquote>
<p data-start="3263" data-end="3331">The difference is not one of degree but of mathematical possibility.</p>
<hr data-start="3333" data-end="3336">
<h2 data-start="3338" data-end="3382"><strong data-start="3341" data-end="3382">8.4 They Are Not Closed Under Scaling</strong></h2>
<p data-start="3384" data-end="3433">Alignment proposals implicitly assume continuity:</p>
<blockquote data-start="3435" data-end="3554">
<p data-start="3437" data-end="3554"><em data-start="3437" data-end="3554">If a system is aligned at 10¹⁰ parameters and 10¹³ FLOPs, it will remain aligned at 10¹³ parameters and 10¹⁶ FLOPs.</em></p>
</blockquote>
<p data-start="3556" data-end="3602">There is no justification for this assumption.</p>
<p data-start="3604" data-end="3649">In fact, almost all current methods scale as:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Alignment&nbsp;stability</mtext><mo>∝</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mtext>Model&nbsp;capability</mtext></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Alignment stability} \propto \frac{1}{\text{Model capability}}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Alignment&nbsp;stability</span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">∝</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 2.2019em; vertical-align: -0.8804em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mopen nulldelimiter"></span><span class="mfrac"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 1.3214em;"><span style="top: -2.314em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Model&nbsp;capability</span></span></span></span><span style="top: -3.23em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="frac-line" style="border-bottom-width: 0.04em;"></span></span><span style="top: -3.677em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">1</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8804em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose nulldelimiter"></span></span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="3727" data-end="3735">because:</p>
<ul data-start="3737" data-end="3915">
<li data-start="3737" data-end="3767">
<p data-start="3739" data-end="3767">oversight capacity saturates</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3768" data-end="3793">
<p data-start="3770" data-end="3793">preference models drift</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3794" data-end="3811">
<p data-start="3796" data-end="3811">proxies overfit</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3812" data-end="3840">
<p data-start="3814" data-end="3840">simulators become schemers</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3841" data-end="3915">
<p data-start="3843" data-end="3915">optimization sharpens the objective beyond the resolution of supervision</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="3917" data-end="3949">RSVP reverses this relationship:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Alignment&nbsp;stability</mtext><mo>∝</mo><mtext>Model&nbsp;capability</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Alignment stability} \propto \text{Model capability}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Alignment&nbsp;stability</span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">∝</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Model&nbsp;capability</span></span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="4017" data-end="4109">because stronger optimization <strong data-start="4047" data-end="4059">tightens</strong> adherence to invariants rather than eroding them.</p>
<hr data-start="4111" data-end="4114">
<h2 data-start="4116" data-end="4211"><strong data-start="4119" data-end="4211">8.5 They Cannot Distinguish Optimization of Values from Optimization of Value-Appearance</strong></h2>
<p data-start="4213" data-end="4438">Every mainstream alignment protocol is compatible with <em data-start="4268" data-end="4284">perfect deceit</em>. A system may satisfy all external criteria while internally optimizing a misaligned objective, provided it models the oversight distribution accurately.</p>
<p data-start="4440" data-end="4535">Formally, given any oversight process <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">O</span></span></span></span>, an optimizing system can learn a dual objective:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><munder><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo></mrow><mi>x</mi></munder><mo fence="false" stretchy="true" minsize="1.8em" maxsize="1.8em">[</mo><mtext>Internal&nbsp;goal</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>⋅</mo><mtext>Predictability-to-oversight</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo fence="false" stretchy="true" minsize="1.8em" maxsize="1.8em">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{x} \Big[ \text{Internal goal}(x) + \lambda \cdot \text{Predictability-to-oversight}(x) \Big]</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.85em; vertical-align: -0.7em;"></span><span class="mop op-limits"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.4306em;"><span style="top: -2.4em; margin-left: 0em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">x</span></span></span></span><span style="top: -3em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span><span class="mop">max</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.7em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="delimsizing size2">[</span></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Internal&nbsp;goal</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">λ</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">⋅</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.8em; vertical-align: -0.65em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Predictability-to-oversight</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mord"><span class="delimsizing size2">]</span></span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="4643" data-end="4738">No behavioral alignment test can distinguish this from genuine alignment, because both produce:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mtext>“aligned”</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(x) = \text{“aligned”}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">O</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">“aligned”</span></span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="4771" data-end="4967">RSVP alignment does not solve this by better oversight, but by <strong data-start="4834" data-end="4925">eliminating representational degrees of freedom in which deceitful equilibria can exist</strong>. Deception requires a divergence between:</p>
<ul data-start="4969" data-end="5040">
<li data-start="4969" data-end="5002">
<p data-start="4971" data-end="5002">the internal objective manifold</p>
</li>
<li data-start="5003" data-end="5040">
<p data-start="5005" data-end="5040">the manifold presented to overseers</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="5042" data-end="5128">RSVP forces these to be the <em data-start="5070" data-end="5127">same manifold with no bifurcation permitted by dynamics</em>.</p>
<hr data-start="5130" data-end="5133">
<h2 data-start="5135" data-end="5200"><strong data-start="5138" data-end="5200">8.6 They Assume Values Can Be Learned Rather Than Required</strong></h2>
<p data-start="5202" data-end="5249">Implicitly, current alignment research assumes:</p>
<blockquote data-start="5251" data-end="5369">
<p data-start="5253" data-end="5369"><em data-start="5253" data-end="5369">There exists a learning process such that, given enough data or feedback, an AI may eventually infer human values.</em></p>
</blockquote>
<p data-start="5371" data-end="5397">RSVP assumes the opposite:</p>
<blockquote data-start="5399" data-end="5538">
<p data-start="5401" data-end="5538"><em data-start="5401" data-end="5538">There must exist a learning process in which no model lacking human-aligned values is reachable by gradient descent in the first place.</em></p>
</blockquote>
<p data-start="5540" data-end="5640">Learning does not discover alignment.<br data-start="5577" data-end="5580">
Learning occurs <strong data-start="5596" data-end="5639">inside alignment-preserving constraints</strong>.</p>
<p data-start="5642" data-end="5673">The difference is foundational:</p>
<div class="_tableContainer_1rjym_1"><div tabindex="-1" class="group _tableWrapper_1rjym_13 flex w-fit flex-col-reverse"><table data-start="5675" data-end="5965" class="w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)"><thead data-start="5675" data-end="5712"><tr data-start="5675" data-end="5712"><th data-start="5675" data-end="5696" data-col-size="sm">Mainstream premise</th><th data-start="5696" data-end="5712" data-col-size="md">RSVP premise</th></tr></thead><tbody data-start="5723" data-end="5965"><tr data-start="5723" data-end="5814"><td data-start="5723" data-end="5752" data-col-size="sm">Learn values from behavior</td><td data-start="5752" data-end="5814" data-col-size="md">Constrain cognition so only aligned values are expressible</td></tr><tr data-start="5815" data-end="5895"><td data-start="5815" data-end="5849" data-col-size="sm">Alignment emerges from training</td><td data-start="5849" data-end="5895" data-col-size="md">Training occurs inside an aligned manifold</td></tr><tr data-start="5896" data-end="5965"><td data-start="5896" data-end="5928" data-col-size="sm">Misalignment must be detected</td><td data-start="5928" data-end="5965" data-col-size="md">Misalignment must be unformulable</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="sticky h-0 select-none end-(--thread-content-margin) self-end"><div class="absolute end-0 flex items-end"><span class="" data-state="closed"><button aria-label="Copy table" class="hover:bg-token-bg-tertiary text-token-text-secondary my-1 rounded-sm p-1 transition-opacity group-[:not(:hover):not(:focus-within)]:pointer-events-none group-[:not(:hover):not(:focus-within)]:opacity-0"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 1