<hr data-start="5967" data-end="5970">
<h2 data-start="5972" data-end="6031"><strong data-start="5975" data-end="6031">8.7 Their Guarantees Are Statistical, Not Structural</strong></h2>
<p data-start="6033" data-end="6079">Existing methods offer statements of the form:</p>
<blockquote data-start="6081" data-end="6154">
<p data-start="6083" data-end="6154"><em data-start="6083" data-end="6154">“The system behaves acceptably on distribution D with probability p.”</em></p>
</blockquote>
<p data-start="6156" data-end="6214">This is not alignment. It is <em data-start="6185" data-end="6213">behavioral risk estimation</em>.</p>
<p data-start="6216" data-end="6243">What alignment requires is:</p>
<blockquote data-start="6245" data-end="6349">
<p data-start="6247" data-end="6349"><em data-start="6247" data-end="6349">“No optimization trajectory reachable under system dynamics can enter a misaligned invariant class.”</em></p>
</blockquote>
<p data-start="6351" data-end="6443">This is not a probability statement.<br data-start="6387" data-end="6390">
It is a <strong data-start="6398" data-end="6442">topological statement about reachability</strong>.</p>
<p data-start="6445" data-end="6543">Only systems satisfying the latter are avoiding misalignment in principle rather than in practice.</p>
<hr data-start="6545" data-end="6548">
<h2 data-start="6550" data-end="6583"><strong data-start="6553" data-end="6583">8.8 Summary of the Impasse</strong></h2>
<div class="_tableContainer_1rjym_1"><div tabindex="-1" class="group _tableWrapper_1rjym_13 flex w-fit flex-col-reverse"><table data-start="6585" data-end="6980" class="w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)"><thead data-start="6585" data-end="6637"><tr data-start="6585" data-end="6637"><th data-start="6585" data-end="6596" data-col-size="sm">Question</th><th data-start="6596" data-end="6619" data-col-size="sm">Mainstream Alignment</th><th data-start="6619" data-end="6637" data-col-size="sm">RSVP Alignment</th></tr></thead><tbody data-start="6652" data-end="6980"><tr data-start="6652" data-end="6695"><td data-start="6652" data-end="6673" data-col-size="sm">What is optimized?</td><td data-start="6673" data-end="6683" data-col-size="sm">Outputs</td><td data-start="6683" data-end="6695" data-col-size="sm">Dynamics</td></tr><tr data-start="6696" data-end="6744"><td data-start="6696" data-end="6719" data-col-size="sm">What is constrained?</td><td data-start="6719" data-end="6730" data-col-size="sm">Behavior</td><td data-start="6730" data-end="6744" data-col-size="sm">Invariants</td></tr><tr data-start="6745" data-end="6788"><td data-start="6745" data-end="6765" data-col-size="sm">What is verified?</td><td data-start="6765" data-end="6775" data-col-size="sm">Samples</td><td data-start="6775" data-end="6788" data-col-size="sm">Structure</td></tr><tr data-start="6789" data-end="6843"><td data-start="6789" data-end="6812" data-col-size="sm">Safety guarantee is…</td><td data-start="6812" data-end="6828" data-col-size="sm">Probabilistic</td><td data-start="6828" data-end="6843" data-col-size="sm">Topological</td></tr><tr data-start="6844" data-end="6917"><td data-start="6844" data-end="6859" data-col-size="sm">Failure mode</td><td data-start="6859" data-end="6885" data-col-size="sm">Undetected misalignment</td><td data-start="6885" data-end="6917" data-col-size="sm">Unrepresentable misalignment</td></tr><tr data-start="6918" data-end="6980"><td data-start="6918" data-end="6935" 