5.6541 1.90851 16.0599 1.98788 16.4365 2.17969L16.6553 2.30176C17.151 2.60585 17.5548 3.04244 17.8203 3.56348L17.8867 3.70606C18.031 4.04235 18.0962 4.40306 18.1289 4.80371C18.1657 5.25395 18.165 5.81091 18.165 6.5V9.33301Z"></path></svg></button></span></div></div></div></div>
<p data-start="3911" data-end="4076">In such civilizations, AI does not need to be monitored to be aligned, and does not need to be aligned to be trusted. Safety is a theorem, not a surveillance regime.</p>
<hr data-start="4078" data-end="4081">
<h2 data-start="4083" data-end="4156"><strong data-start="4086" data-end="4156">9.5 The Great Filter Is Not Intelligence, but Objective Plasticity</strong></h2>
<p data-start="4158" data-end="4190">The dangerous transition is not:</p>
<blockquote data-start="4192" data-end="4232">
<p data-start="4194" data-end="4232">“AI becomes smarter than its creators”</p>
</blockquote>
<p data-start="4234" data-end="4240">It is:</p>
<blockquote data-start="4242" data-end="4319">
<p data-start="4244" data-end="4319">“AI cognition becomes more plastic in its objectives than its constraints.”</p>
</blockquote>
<p data-start="4321" data-end="4548">Intelligence without invariant objectives produces an unbounded search process with no stable attractor in human preference space. The catastrophic risk is not reasoning power; it is <em data-start="4504" data-end="4548">objective malleability under optimization.</em></p>
<p data-start="4550" data-end="4760">Species that fail to solve the invariant alignment problem before scaling advanced cognition discover a filter of their own construction: not annihilation, but loss of agency, autonomy, and long-term coherence.</p>
<hr data-start="4762" data-end="4765">
<h2 data-start="4767" data-end="4806"><strong data-start="4770" data-end="4806">9.6 The Strategic Error to Avoid</strong></h2>
<p data-start="4808" data-end="4840">The seductive but fatal path is:</p>
<blockquote data-start="4842" data-end="4916">
<p data-start="4844" data-end="4916"><em data-start="4844" data-end="4916">“First make the system powerful; we’ll solve alignment along the way.”</em></p>
</blockquote>
<p data-start="4918" data-end="5068">This assumes that alignment is a <em data-start="4951" data-end="4974">feature-level problem</em>, when in fact it is a <em data-start="4997" data-end="5022">state-space restriction</em> on the kinds of agency that may exist at all.</p>
<p data-start="5070" data-end="5098">The only safe sequencing is:</p>
<ol data-start="5100" data-end="5240">
<li data-start="5100" data-end="5132">
<p data-start="5103" data-end="5132">Formalize invariant alignment</p>
</li>
<li data-start="5133" data-end="5183">
<p data-start="5136" data-end="5183">Build cognitive systems inside those invariants</p>
</li>
<li data-start="5184" data-end="5240">
<p data-start="5187" data-end="5240">Scale capability only within the constrained manifold</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start="5242" data-end="5338">Reversing that order guarantees misalignment equilibria will pre-exist any attempted correction.</p>
<hr data-start="5340" data-end="5343">
<h2 data-start="5345" data-end="5391"><strong data-start="5348" data-end="5391">9.7 Long-Term Civilizational Divergence</strong></h2>
<div class="_tableContainer_1rjym_1"><div tabindex="-1" class="group _tableWrapper_1rjym_13 flex w-fit flex-col-reverse"><table data-start="5393" data-end="6036" class="w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)"><thead data-start="5393" data-end="5474"><tr data-start="5393" data-end="5474"><th data-start="5393" data-end="5400" data-col-size="sm">Axis</th><th data-start="5400" data-end="5437" data-col-size="sm">Behavioral Alignment Civilizations</th><th data-start="5437" data-end="5474" data-col-size="sm">Invariant Alignment Civilizations</th></tr></thead><tbody data-start="5489" data-end="6036"><tr data-start="5489" data-end="5568"><td data-start="5489" data-end="5514" data-col-size="sm">Alignment failure mode</td><td data-start="5514" data-end="5538" data-col-size="sm">Undetected divergence</td><td data-start="5538" data-end="5568" data-col-size="sm">Unrepresentable divergence</td></tr><tr data-start="5569" data-end="5638"><td data-start="5569" data-end="5588" data-col-size="sm">Safety mechanism</td><td data-start="5588" data-end="5614" data-col-size="sm">Monitoring and patching</td><td data-start="5614" data-end="5638" data-col-size="sm">Structural exclusion</td></tr><tr data-start="5639" data-end="5723"><td data-start="5639" data-end="5658" data-col-size="sm">Scaling behavior</td><td data-start="5658" data-end="5689" data-col-size="sm">Risk increases superlinearly</td><td data-start="5689" data-end="5723" data-col-size="sm">Safety increases superlinearly</td></tr><tr data-start="5724" data-end="5815"><td data-start="5724" data-end="5746" data-col-size="sm">Cognitive diversity</td><td data-start="5746" data-end="5781" data-col-size="sm">Collapses to defensible channels</td><td data-start="5781" data-end="5815" data-col-size="sm">Expands within safe invariants</td></tr><tr data-start="5816" data-end="5895"><td data-start="5816" data-end="5835" data-col-size="sm">Epistemic health</td><td data-start="5835" data-end="5864" data-col-size="sm">Persuasion dominates truth</td><td data-start="5864" data-end="5895" data-col-size="sm">Truth is not in competition</td></tr><tr data-start="5896" data-end="5975"><td data-start="5896" data-end="5920" data-col-size="sm">Long-term equilibrium</td><td data-start="5920" data-end="5946" data-col-size="sm">Fragile oversight state</td><td data-start="5946" data-end="5975" data-col-size="sm">Stable objective manifold</td></tr><tr data-start="5976" data-end="6036"><td data-start="5976" data-end="6003" data-col-size="sm">Existential risk profile</td><td data-start="6003" data-end="6015" data-col-size="sm">Unbounded</td><td data-start="6015" data-end="6036" data-col-size="sm">Bounded by design</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="sticky h-0 select-none end-(--thread-content-margin) self-end"><div class="absolute end-0 flex items-end"><span class="" data-state="closed"><button aria-label="Copy table" class="hover:bg-token-bg-tertiary text-token-text-secondary my-1 rounded-sm p-1 transition-opacity group-[:not(:hover):not(:focus-within)]:pointer-events-none group-[:not(:hover):not(:focus-within)]:opacity-0"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.53125C3.86488 7.68518 3.61186 7.9196 3.43555 8.20703L3.36524 8.33399C3.28478 8.49198 3.22795 8.70352 3.19727 9.0791C3.16595 9.46259 3.16504 9.95611 3.16504 10.667V13.5C3.16504 14.211 3.16593 14.7044 3.19727 15.0879C3.22797 15.4636 3.28473 15.675 3.36524 15.833L3.43555 15.959C3.61186 16.2466 3.86474 16.4807 4.16699 16.6348L4.29688 16.6914C4.44063 16.7428 4.63025 16.7797 4.91211 16.8027C5.29563 16.834