markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="270">Here is a <strong data-start="10" data-end="65">clear, precise, non-boilerplate set of instructions</strong> for how to extend and complete this LaTeX paper without rewriting it for you. These target structure, rigor, missing technical content, and places where the arguments must be made mathematically explicit.</p>
<hr data-start="272" data-end="275">
<h1 data-start="277" data-end="343">✅ <strong data-start="281" data-end="343">Instructions for Extending and Completing This LaTeX Draft</strong></h1>
<hr data-start="345" data-end="348">
<h2 data-start="350" data-end="383"><strong data-start="353" data-end="383">1. Strengthen the Abstract</strong></h2>
<p data-start="384" data-end="396"><strong data-start="384" data-end="396">Do this:</strong></p>
<ul data-start="397" data-end="612">
<li data-start="397" data-end="612">
<p data-start="399" data-end="428">Add 2–3 sentences that state:</p>
<ul data-start="431" data-end="612">
<li data-start="431" data-end="481">
<p data-start="433" data-end="481"><em data-start="433" data-end="449">What is proven</em> (invariant fixed point theorem)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="484" data-end="545">
<p data-start="486" data-end="545"><em data-start="486" data-end="507">What is constructed</em> (RSVP-aligned cognitive architecture)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="548" data-end="612">
<p data-start="550" data-end="612"><em data-start="550" data-end="569">What is predicted</em> (failure modes of non-invariant alignment)</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="614" data-end="654"><strong data-start="614" data-end="654">Check that the abstract now answers:</strong></p>
<ol data-start="655" data-end="807">
<li data-start="655" data-end="696">
<p data-start="658" data-end="696">What is wrong with existing alignment?</p>
</li>
<li data-start="697" data-end="734">
<p data-start="700" data-end="734">What is the invariant alternative?</p>
</li>
<li data-start="735" data-end="769">
<p data-start="738" data-end="769">What formal result is achieved?</p>
</li>
<li data-start="770" data-end="807">
<p data-start="773" data-end="807">What implication follows at scale?</p>
</li>
</ol>
<hr data-start="809" data-end="812">
<h2 data-start="814" data-end="847"><strong data-start="817" data-end="847">2. Expand the Introduction</strong></h2>
<p data-start="848" data-end="889">Add short subsections or paragraphs that:</p>
<ul data-start="891" data-end="1155">
<li data-start="891" data-end="989">
<p data-start="893" data-end="989">Define <strong data-start="900" data-end="913">alignment</strong>, <strong data-start="915" data-end="929">invariance</strong>, and <strong data-start="935" data-end="958">objective structure</strong> precisely (one paragraph each)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="990" data-end="1155">
<p data-start="992" data-end="1015">Explicitly distinguish:</p>
<ul data-start="1018" data-end="1155">
<li data-start="1018" data-end="1065">
<p data-start="1020" data-end="1065"><em data-start="1020" data-end="1065">behavioral alignment vs objective alignment</em></p>
</li>
<li data-start="1068" data-end="1109">
<p data-start="1070" data-end="1109"><em data-start="1070" data-end="1109">empirical safety vs structural safety</em></p>
</li>
<li data-start="1112" data-end="1155">
<p data-start="1114" data-end="1155"><em data-start="1114" data-end="1155">reward alignment vs invariant alignment</em></p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1157" data-end="1208">Add a short <em data-start="1169" data-end="1188">roadmap paragraph</em> ending the section:</p>
<blockquote data-start="1210" data-end="1267">
<p data-start="1212" data-end="1267">“The remainder of this paper is structured as follows…”</p>
</blockquote>
<p data-start="1269" data-end="1307">listing sections 2–10 in one sentence.</p>
<hr data-start="1309" data-end="1312">
<h2 data-start="1314" data-end="1377"><strong data-start="1317" data-end="1377">3. Add One Diagram-Free but Formal “Concept Map” in Text</strong></h2>
<p data-start="1379" data-end="1475">After Section 3, add a small paragraph stating equivalences in prose rather than graphics, e.g.:</p>
<blockquote data-start="1477" data-end="1728">
<p data-start="1479" data-end="1728">“Invariant alignment may be expressed equivalently as:<br>
(1) dynamical flow constrained by entropy geometry,<br>
(2) functorial preservation of value stacks under updating,<br>
(3) compression to fixed objective generators invariant under optimization.”</p>
</blockquote>
<hr data-start="1730" data-end="1733">
<h2 data-start="1735" data-end="1781"><strong data-start="1738" data-end="1781">4. Expand the Core Theorem Section (7A)</strong></h2>
<p data-start="1782" data-end="1837">Inside <strong data-start="1789" data-end="1795">7A</strong>, insert the following missing components:</p>
<h3 data-start="1839" data-end="1891">(a) Define the optimization semigroup explicitly</h3>
<p data-start="1892" data-end="1896">Add:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∘</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo separator="true">,</mo><mspace width="1em"></mspace><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">d</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{t+s} = U_t \circ U_s, \quad U_0 = \mathrm{id}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8917em; vertical-align: -0.2083em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">U</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2806em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.109em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span><span class="mbin mtight">+</span><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">s</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2083em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8333em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">U</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2806em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.109em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">∘</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8778em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">U</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.1514em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.109em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">s</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 1em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">U</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.109em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">0</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6944em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathrm">id</span></span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="1954" data-end="2050">Explain in one sentence that capability growth is modeled as a semigroup, not a discrete update.</p>
<h3 data-start="2052" data-end="2104">(b) Add a short proof sketch of the main theorem</h3>
<p data-start="2105" data-end="2132">Under the theorem, include:</p>
<ul data-start="2134" data-end="2384">
<li data-start="2134" data-end="2287">
<p data-start="2136" data-end="2287"><em data-start="2136" data-end="2151">Idea of proof</em>: invariants define equivalence classes; optimization acts within equivalence classes iff its generator lies in the stabilizer subgroup.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2288" data-end="2384">
<p data-start="2290" data-end="2384"><em data-start="2290" data-end="2303">Consequence</em>: alignment reduces to proving the generator of <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_t</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8333em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">U</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2806em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.109em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> lies in that Lie algebra.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="2386" data-end="2439">(No need for full rigor—just 5–7 lines of reasoning.)</p>
<h3 data-start="2441" data-end="2491">(c) Add explicit obstruction characterization:</h3>
