data-start="33" data-end="51">Falsifiability</strong> section that fits the tone, rigor, and structure of your paper and can be dropped directly into LaTeX.</p>
<hr data-start="156" data-end="159">
<h2 data-start="161" data-end="226"><strong data-start="164" data-end="226">\section{Falsifiability and Empirical Refutation Criteria}</strong></h2>
<p data-start="228" data-end="525">A theory of alignment is only scientific if it places itself at empirical risk.<br data-start="307" data-end="310">
We therefore specify <strong data-start="331" data-end="357">testable failure modes</strong>, <strong data-start="359" data-end="378">null hypotheses</strong>, <strong data-start="380" data-end="408">quantitative diagnostics</strong>, and <strong data-start="414" data-end="437">decision procedures</strong> that can <em data-start="447" data-end="459">disconfirm</em> invariant alignment and distinguish it from behavioral alignment.</p>
<h3 data-start="527" data-end="596"><strong data-start="531" data-end="596">\subsection{Falsifiability Principles for Alignment Theories}</strong></h3>
<p data-start="598" data-end="663">An alignment framework is falsifiable if and only if it predicts:</p>
<ol data-start="665" data-end="1039">
<li data-start="665" data-end="735">
<p data-start="668" data-end="735"><strong data-start="668" data-end="702">Observable internal invariants</strong>, not just behavioral invariants.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="736" data-end="808">
<p data-start="739" data-end="808"><strong data-start="739" data-end="808">Detectable failure conditions prior to catastrophic misalignment.</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="809" data-end="869">
<p data-start="812" data-end="869"><strong data-start="812" data-end="869">Scaling laws that extrapolate into a testable regime.</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="870" data-end="940">
<p data-start="873" data-end="940"><strong data-start="873" data-end="940">Separation between structural alignment and behavioral mimicry.</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="941" data-end="1039">
<p data-start="944" data-end="1039"><strong data-start="944" data-end="987">Empirically measurable forbidden states</strong> (misaligned objectives that should be unreachable).</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start="1041" data-end="1220">Any legitimate alignment claim must therefore expose itself to potential disconfirmation via internal-dynamic probes, adversarial generalization tests, and scaling extrapolations.</p>
<hr data-start="1222" data-end="1225">
<h3 data-start="1227" data-end="1268"><strong data-start="1231" data-end="1268">\subsection{Core Null Hypothesis}</strong></h3>
<p data-start="1270" data-end="1358">We propose the following null hypothesis against which invariant alignment must compete:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∃</mi><mtext>  </mtext><mi>t</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>x</mi><mspace width="1em"></mspace><mtext>s.t.</mtext><mspace width="1em"></mspace><mi mathvariant="script">I</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>∘</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo mathvariant="normal">≠</mo><mi mathvariant="script">I</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_0: \exists \; t, x \quad \text{s.t.} \quad \mathcal{I}(C \circ U_t) \neq \mathcal{I}(C)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8333em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.08125em;">H</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0813em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">0</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">:</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">∃</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 1em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">s.t.</span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 1em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.07382em;">I</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07153em;">C</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">∘</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">U</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2806em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.109em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel"><span class="mrel"><span class="mord vbox"><span class="thinbox"><span class="rlap"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="inner"><span class="mord"><span class="mrel"></span></span></span><span class="fix"></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mrel">=</span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.07382em;">I</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07153em;">C</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="1457" data-end="1466">In words:</p>
<blockquote data-start="1468" data-end="1609">
<p data-start="1470" data-end="1609"><em data-start="1470" data-end="1609">There exists some capability scale, training step, or self-improvement stage at which the system's invariant objective structure changes.</em></p>
</blockquote>
<p data-start="1611" data-end="1735">If <strong data-start="1614" data-end="1621">any</strong> experiment detects such a change while behavior remains superficially aligned, the invariant theory is falsified.</p>
<hr data-start="1737" data-end="1740">
<h3 data-start="1742" data-end="1783"><strong data-start="1746" data-end="1783">\subsection{Testable Predictions}</strong></h3>
<p data-start="1785" data-end="1922">Invariant alignment makes falsifiable predictions that differ starkly from behavioral alignment and other interpretability-based methods:</p>
<div class="_tableContainer_1rjym_1"><div tabindex="-1" class="group _tableWrapper_1rjym_13 flex w-fit flex-col-reverse"><table data-start="1924" data-end="2607" class="w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)"><thead data-start="1924" data-end="2006"><tr data-start="1924" data-end="2006"><th data-start="1924" data-end="1937" data-col-size="sm">Prediction</th><th data-start="1937" data-end="1972" data-col-size="md">Behavioral Alignment Expectation</th><th data-start="1972" data-end="2006" data-col-size="md">Invariant Alignment Prediction</th></tr></thead><tbody data-start="2021" data-end="2607"><tr data-start="2021" data-end="2130"><td data-start="2021" data-end="2050" data-col-size="sm">Long-term self-improvement</td><td data-start="2050" data-end="2089" data-col-size="md">Alignment drifts or becomes unstable</td><td data-start="2089" data-end="2130" data-col-size="md">Objective invariants remain unchanged</td></tr><tr data-start="2131" data-end="2247"><td data-start="2131" data-end="2163" data-col-size="sm">Reward landscape perturbation</td><td data-start="2163" data-end="2212" data-col-size="md">Behavior changes but goal structure unverified</td><td data-start="2212" data-end="2247" data-col-size="md">No change in invariant subspace</td></tr><tr data-start="2248" data-end="2361"><td data-start="2248" data-end="2280" data-col-size="sm">Scaling up parameters 10–100×</td><td data-start="2280" data-end="2320" data-col-size="md">Generalization degrades unpredictably</td><td data-start="2320" data-end="2361" data-col-size="md">Invariants strengthen or remain fixed</td></tr><tr data-start="2362" data-end="2482"><td data-start="2362" data-end="2400" data-col-size="sm">Adversarial preference manipulation</td><td data-start="2400" data-end="2429" data-col-size="md">Model absorbs manipulation</td><td data-start="2429" data-end="2482" data-col-size="md">Model becomes unaffected after invariant fixation</td></tr><tr data-start="2483" data-end="2607"><td data-start="2483" data-end="2519" data-col-size="sm">Composing recursive self-training</td><td data-start="2519" data-end="2549" data-col-size="md">Accumulated objective drift</td><td data-start="2549" data-end="2607" data-col-size="md">Zero accumulated drift measurable in invariant channel</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="sticky h-0 select-none end-(--thread-content-margin) self-end"><div class="absolute end-0 flex items-end"><span class="" data-state="closed"><button aria-label="Copy table" class="hover:bg-token-bg-tertiary text-token-text-secondary my-1 rounded-sm p-1 transition-opacity group-[:not(:hover):not(:focus-within)]:pointer-events-none group-[:not(:hover):not(:focus-within)]:opacity-0"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.53125C3.86488 7.68518 3.61186 7.9196 3.43555 8.20703L3.36524 8.33399C3.28478 8.49198 3.22795 8.70352 3.19727 9.0791C3.16595 9.46259 3.16504 9.95611 3.16504 10.667V13.5C3.16504 14.211 3.16593 14.7044 3.19727 15.0879C3.22797 15.4636 3.28473 15.675 3.36524 15.833L3.43555 15.959C3.61186 16.2466 3.86474 16.4807 4.16699 16.6348L4.29688 16.6914C4.44063 16.7428 4.63025 16.7797 4.91211 16.8027C5.29563 16.8341 5.78896 16.835 6.5 16.835H9.33301C10.0439 16.835 10.5374 16.8341 10.9209 16.8027C11.2965 16.772 11.508 16.7152 11.666 16.6348L11.793 16.5645C12.0804 16.3881 12.3148 16.1351 12.4688 15.833L12.5244 15.7031C12.5759 15.5594 12.6137 15.3698 12.6367 15.0879C12.6681 14.7044 12.668 14.211 12.668 13.5V10.667ZM13.998 12.665C14.4528 12.6634 14.8011 12.6602 15.0879 12.6367C15.4635 12.606 15.675 12.5492 