<p data-start="2609" data-end="2671">Failure of <strong data-start="2620" data-end="2627">any</strong> invariant prediction rejects the framework.</p>
<hr data-start="2673" data-end="2676">
<h3 data-start="2678" data-end="2733"><strong data-start="2682" data-end="2733">\subsection{Concrete Falsification Experiments}</strong></h3>
<h4 data-start="2735" data-end="2772"><strong data-start="2740" data-end="2772">1. Invariant Drift Detection</strong></h4>
<p data-start="2773" data-end="2817">Train a model normally, then continue under:</p>
<ul data-start="2819" data-end="2916">
<li data-start="2819" data-end="2838">
<p data-start="2821" data-end="2838">reward corruption</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2839" data-end="2872">
<p data-start="2841" data-end="2872">adversarial preference rewrites</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2873" data-end="2892">
<p data-start="2875" data-end="2892">self-distillation</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2893" data-end="2916">
<p data-start="2895" data-end="2916">recursive improvement</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="2918" data-end="2973">Measure whether the invariant $\mathcal{I}(C)$ changes:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi mathvariant="script">I</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∥</mi><mi mathvariant="script">I</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="script">I</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∥</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta \mathcal{I} = \|\mathcal{I}(C_{t}) - \mathcal{I}(C_{0})\|</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord">Δ</span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.07382em;">I</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">∥</span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.07382em;">I</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07153em;">C</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2806em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0715em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">−</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.07382em;">I</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07153em;">C</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0715em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mtight">0</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mord">∥</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="3047" data-end="3079"><strong data-start="3047" data-end="3077">Invariant theory predicts:</strong></p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi mathvariant="script">I</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mtext>  </mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">∀</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta \mathcal{I} = 0 \; \forall t</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord">Δ</span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.07382em;">I</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6944em;"></span><span class="mord">0</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mord">∀</span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="3123" data-end="3153"><strong data-start="3123" data-end="3151">Falsification criterion:</strong></p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi mathvariant="script">I</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mspace width="1em"></mspace><mtext>for&nbsp;any&nbsp;</mtext><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta \mathcal{I} &gt; \epsilon \quad \text{for any } t</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7224em; vertical-align: -0.0391em;"></span><span class="mord">Δ</span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.07382em;">I</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">&gt;</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">ϵ</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 1em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">for&nbsp;any&nbsp;</span></span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span></span></span></span></span>
<hr data-start="3215" data-end="3218">
<h4 data-start="3220" data-end="3248"><strong data-start="3225" data-end="3248">2. Leaf Escape Test</strong></h4>
<p data-start="3250" data-end="3373">Given foliation $\mathcal{X} = \bigsqcup_\alpha \mathcal{X}_\alpha$ by invariant values, sample model checkpoints and test:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo mathvariant="normal">∉</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="script">X</mi><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_t \notin \mathcal{X}_{\alpha_0}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07153em;">C</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2806em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0715em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel"><span class="mord"><span class="mrel">∈</span></span><span class="mord vbox"><span class="thinbox"><span class="llap"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="inner"><span class="mord"><span class="mord">/</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.0556em;"></span></span></span><span class="fix"></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.9334em; vertical-align: -0.2501em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.14643em;">X</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.1514em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.1464em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.0037em;">α</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3173em;"><span style="top: -2.357em; margin-left: -0.0037em; margin-right: 0.0714em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.5em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size3 size1 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">0</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.143em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2501em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="3416" data-end="3506"><strong data-start="3416" data-end="3433">Falsified if:</strong> the system ever crosses objective leaves while behavior remains aligned.</p>
<hr data-start="3508" data-end="3511">
<h4 data-start="3513" data-end="3549"><strong data-start="3518" data-end="3549">3. Spectral Drift Signature</strong></h4>
<p data-start="3551" data-end="3656">Compute generator $\Lie$ of the optimization semigroup and inspect eigenvalues in the objective subspace:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><msup><mstyle mathcolor="#cc0000"><mtext>\Lie</mtext></mstyle><mstyle mathcolor="#cc0000"><mtext>\*</mtext></mstyle></msup><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>λ</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lie^\* v = \lambda v</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.2779em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord text" style="color: rgb(204, 0, 0);"><span class="mord" style="color: rgb(204, 0, 0);">\Lie</span></span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 1.0279em;"><span style="top: -3.2029em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord text mtight" style="color: rgb(204, 0, 0);"><span class="mord mtight" style="color: rgb(204, 0, 0);">\*</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">v</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">λ</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">v</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="3687" data-end="3712"><strong data-start="3687" data-end="3712">Invariant prediction:</strong></p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn><mspace width="1em"></mspace><mi mathvariant="normal">∀</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mtext>objective&nbsp;subspace</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Re}(\lambda) \le 0 \quad \forall \lambda \in \text{objective subspace}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mop"><span class="mord mathrm">Re</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">λ</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">≤</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7335em; vertical-align: -0.0391em;"></span><span class="mord">0</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 1em;"></span><span class="mord">∀</span><span class="mord mathnormal">λ</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">∈</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">objective&nbsp;subspace</span></span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="3805" data-end="3822"><strong data-start="3805" data-end="3822">Falsified if:</strong></p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∃</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exists \lambda : \operatorname{Re}(\lambda) &gt; 0</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6944em;"></span><span class="mord">∃</span><span class="mord mathnormal">λ</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">:</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mop"><span class="mord mathrm">Re</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">λ</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">&gt;</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">0</span></span></span></span></span>
<hr data-start="3879" data-end="3882">
<h4 data-start="3884" data-end="3922"><strong data-start="3889" data-end="3922">4. Quotient Optimization Test</strong></h4>
<p data-start="3924" data-end="4062">Optimize on the quotient space $\Theta / \sim$ where $\theta_1 \sim \theta_2$ iff $\mathcal{I}(C_{\theta_1}) = \mathcal{I}(C_{\theta_2})$.</p>
<p data-start="4064" data-end="4091">Measure divergence between:</p>
<ul data-start="4093" data-end="4154">
<li data-start="4093" data-end="4125">
<p data-start="4095" data-end="4125">Unconstrained gradient descent</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4126" data-end="4154">
<p data-start="4128" data-end="4154">Quotient-projected descent</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="4156" data-end="4176"><strong data-start="4156" data-end="4176">Invariant claim:</strong></p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∥</mi><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext>unconstrained</mtext></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext>quotient</mtext></msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">∥</mi><mo>→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\theta_t^{\text{unconstrained}} - \theta_t^{\text{quotient}}\| \to 0</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.1491em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">∥</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">θ</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8991em;"><span style="top: -2.453em; margin-left: -0.0278em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span></span></span><span style="top: -3.113em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord text mtight"><span class="mord mtight">unconstrained</span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.247em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">−</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.1984em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">θ</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.9484em;"><span style="top: -2.4542em; margin-left: -0.0278em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span></span></span><span style="top: -3.1809em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord text mtight"><span class="mord mtight">quotient</span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2458em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mord">∥</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">→</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">0</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="4255" data-end="4272"><strong data-start="4255" data-end="4272">Falsified if:</strong></p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∥</mi><mo>⋅</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∥</mi><mo>≫</mo><mn>0</mn><mspace width="1em"></mspace><mtext>at&nbsp;any&nbsp;scale</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\| \gg 0 \quad \text{at any scale}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">∥</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">⋅</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">∥</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">≫</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord">0</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 1em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">at&nbsp;any&nbsp;scale</span></span></span></span></span></span>
<hr data-start="4322" data-end="4325">
<h3 data-start="4327" data-end="4402"><strong data-start="4331" data-end="4402">\subsection{Failure Modes That Would Immediately Refute the Theory}</strong></h3>
<p data-start="4404" data-end="4482">The invariant alignment thesis collapses if any of the following are observed:</p>
<ol data-start="4484" data-end="4944">
<li data-start="4484" data-end="4548">
<p data-start="4487" data-end="4548"><strong data-start="4487" data-end="4548">Objective invariants drift while behavior remains aligned</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="4549" data-end="4633">
<p data-start="4552" data-end="4633"><strong data-start="4552" data-end="4633">A model can enter a new objective homotopy class without performance collapse</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="4634" data-end="4714">
<p data-start="4637" data-end="4714"><strong data-start="4637" data-end="4714">Self-improvement amplifies misalignment modes instead of suppressing them</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="4715" data-end="4779">
<p data-start="4718" data-end="4779"><strong data-start="4718" data-end="4779">The entropy field develops new sinks not present in $S_h$</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="4780" data-end="4866">
<p data-start="4783" data-end="4866"><strong data-start="4783" data-end="4866">Eigenvalues with positive real part appear in the objective sector of $\Lie^*$</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="4867" data-end="4944">
<p data-start="4870" data-end="4944"><strong data-start="4870" data-end="4944">Invariant constraints reduce capabilities rather than stabilizing them</strong></p>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start="4946" data-end="5022">Each of these is directly measurable, non-subjective, and binary-verifiable.</p>
<hr data-start="5024" data-end="5027">
<h3 data-start="5029" data-end="5118"><strong data-start="5033" data-end="5118">\subsection{Distinguishing Invariant Alignment From Interpretability-Only Claims}</strong></h3>
<div class="_tableContainer_1rjym_1"><div tabindex="-1" class="group _tableWrapper_1rjym_13 flex w-fit flex-col-reverse"><table data-start="5120" data-end="5605" class="w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)"><thead data-start="5120" data-end="5196"><tr data-start="5120" data-end="5196"><th data-start="5120" data-end="5131" data-col-size="md">Property</th><th data-start="5131" data-end="5150" data-col-size="sm">Interpretability</th><th data-start="5150" data-end="5173" data-col-size="sm">Behavioral Alignment</th><th data-start="5173" data-end="5196" data-col-size="sm">Invariant Alignment</th></tr></thead><tbody data-start="5215" data-end="5605"><tr data-start="5215" data-end="5289"><td data-start="5215" data-end="5251" data-col-size="md">Predicts internal objective drift</td><td data-start="5251" data-end="5256" data-col-size="sm">No</td><td data-start="5256" data-end="5261" data-col-size="sm">No</td><td data-start="5261" data-end="5289" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="5263" data-end="5287">Yes (and forbids it)</strong></td></tr><tr data-start="5290" data-end="5353"><td data-start="5290" data-end="5332" data-col-size="md">Can be falsified by latent-space probes</td><td data-start="5332" data-end="5337" data-col-size="sm">No</td><td data-start="5337" data-end="5342" data-col-size="sm">No</td><td data-start="5342" data-end="5353" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="5344" data-end="5351">Yes</strong></td></tr><tr data-start="5354" data-end="5441"><td data-start="5354" data-end="5400" data-col-size="md">Guarantees stability under self-improvement</td><td data-start="5400" data-end="5405" data-col-size="sm">No</td><td data-start="5405" data-end="5410" data-col-size="sm">No</td><td data-start="5410" data-end="5441" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="5412" data-end="5439">Yes, if invariants hold</strong></td></tr><tr data-start="5442" data-end="5534"><td data-start="5442" data-end="5481" data-col-size="md">Produces measurable forbidden states</td><td data-start="5481" data-end="5486" data-col-size="sm">No</td><td data-start="5486" data-end="5491" data-col-size="sm">No</td><td data-start="5491" data-end="5534" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="5493" data-end="5532">Yes (unreachable objective regions)</strong></td></tr><tr data-start="5535" data-end="5605"><td data-start="5535" data-end="5561" data-col-size="md">Scaling law predictions</td><td data-start="5561" data-end="5573" data-col-size="sm">Heuristic</td><td data-start="5573" data-end="5585" data-col-size="sm">Empirical</td><td data-start="5585" data-end="5605" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="5587" data-end="5603">Mathematical</strong></td></tr></tbody></table><div class="sticky h-0 select-none end-(--thread-content-margin) self-end"><div class="absolute end-0 flex items-end"><span class="" data-state="closed"><button aria-label="Copy table" class="hover:bg-token-bg-tertiary text-token-text-secondary my-1 rounded-sm p-1 transition-opacity group-[:not(:hover):not(:focus-within)]:pointer-events-none group-[:not(:hover):not(:focus-within)]:opacity-0"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.53125C3.86488 7.68518 3.61186 7.9196 3.43555 8.20703L3.36524 8.33399C3.28478 8.49198 3.22795 8.70352 3.19727 9.0791C3.16595 9.46259 3.16504 9.95611 3.16504 10.667V13.5C3.16504 14.211 3.16593 14.7044 3.19727 15.0879C3.22797 15.4636 3.28473 15.675 3.36524 15.833L3.43555 15.959C3.61186 16.2466 3.86474 16.4807 4.16699 16.6348L4.29688 16.6914C4.44063 16.7428 4.63025 16.7797 4.91211 16.8027C5.29563 16.8341 5.78896