<hr data-start="6111" data-end="6114">
<h3 data-start="6116" data-end="6157">**\subsection{Provisional Conclusion}</h3>
<p data-start="6159" data-end="6262">Unlike behavioral alignment, the invariant alignment framework exposes itself to falsification through:</p>
<ul data-start="6264" data-end="6418">
<li data-start="6264" data-end="6300">
<p data-start="6266" data-end="6300"><strong data-start="6266" data-end="6300">internal objective measurement</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="6301" data-end="6324">
<p data-start="6303" data-end="6324"><strong data-start="6303" data-end="6324">spectral dynamics</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="6325" data-end="6359">
<p data-start="6327" data-end="6359"><strong data-start="6327" data-end="6359">quotient learning divergence</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="6360" data-end="6386">
<p data-start="6362" data-end="6386"><strong data-start="6362" data-end="6386">leaf escape topology</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="6387" data-end="6418">
<p data-start="6389" data-end="6418"><strong data-start="6389" data-end="6418">entropy geometry failures</strong></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="6420" data-end="6518">This makes it a <em data-start="6436" data-end="6517">Popper-compliant scientific hypothesis rather than an aspirational safety claim</em>.</p>
<hr data-start="6520" data-end="6523">
<p data-start="6525" data-end="6578">If you want, I can now generate any of the following:</p>
<ol data-start="6580" data-end="6903">
